- button:\n      - button:\n        - paragraph: 让我深入查看几个关键来源，获取更详细的专利布局信息。\n      - button:\n        - generic: 执行了 3 个操作 · dynamic__web_fetch · dynamic__fetch_url\n      - button:\n      - paragraph: 继续研究 Eight Sleep 专利布局方向。\n      - button:\n      - button:\n      - button:\n      - button:\n      - generic: Kane\n      - generic: 队长\n      - button [expanded]:\n        - generic: 收起过程回放\n      - button:\n        - generic: 执行了 12 个操作 · dynamic__platform_search · dynamic__web_search · dynamic__platform_read +1\n      - button:\n      - button:\n        - generic: dynamic__fetch_url\n      - button:\n        - generic: dynamic__fetch_url\n      - button:\n        - generic: dynamic__platform_search\n      - button:\n        - generic: dynamic__web_search\n      - button:\n        - generic: dynamic__fetch_url\n      - button:\n        - generic: dynamic__fetch_url\n      - button:\n        - generic: dynamic__platform_read\n      - button:\n        - generic: dynamic__platform_read\n      - button:\n        - generic: dynamic__web_search\n      - button:\n        - generic: dynamic__web_search\n      - button:\n        - generic: dynamic__fetch_url\n      - button:\n        - generic: dynamic__web_search\n      - paragraph: 已收集到足够信息，以下是研究结论。\n      - paragraph: Eight Sleep 专利布局方向研究\n      - list:\n        - code: \"57\"\n        - text: 件全球专利、\n        - code: \"6\"\n        - text: 个核心专利家族、\n        - code: \"26\"\n        - text: 件有效（GreyB 2024 统计）；2021 年约\n        - code: \"28\"\n        - text: 件专利资产，组合随 Pod 产品迭代持续扩张。\n        - text: 核心发明人：\n        - code: Matteo Franceschetti\n        - text: 、\n        - code: Massimo Andreasi Bassi\n        - text: ；最被引用专利\n        - code: US20150355612A1\n        - text: ，被 Fitbit、LG 等引用\n        - code: \"139\"\n        - text: 次。\n      - paragraph: 核心布局方向\n      - list:\n        - code: 水循环温控系统\n        - text: ：最核心护城河，覆盖 Pod 的水冷/加热 Hub、床面温度动态调节、睡眠周期分阶段控温曲线、湿度控制。\n        - code: 双人分区独立控温\n        - text: ：左右分区独立加热/制冷，解决同床异温需求，是与竞品差异化的关键权利要求。\n        - code: 非穿戴生理信号采集\n        - text: ：床垫传感器条采集心率、呼吸、体温、体动；鼾声/睡眠呼吸暂停特征频率检测。\n        - code: 闭环智能控制\n        - text: ：基于生理信号分析反控床具（温度、床头抬升止鼾、支撑硬度），对应\n        - code: US11,904,103\n        - text: （Sleep Pod，2024 授权）与\n        - code: US12,370,339\n        - text: （多用户可调床，2025 授权）。\n        - code: 智能交互与生态\n        - text: ：App 学习用户偏好、Alexa/智能家居联动、振动/温度智能唤醒闹钟。\n      - paragraph: 近期动向\n      - list:\n        - code: AI 化\n        - text: ：2025 年推出 Autopilot 4.0（AI 睡眠代理，结合日间活动预测夜间温控），预计后续申请向算法/Agent 控制逻辑倾斜。\n        - code: 主动维权\n        - text: ：2025 年 10 月在加州中区起诉 Orion Longevity（\n        - code: 2:25-cv-09685\n        - text: ），主张\n        - code: ’461\n        - text: 、\n        - code: ’240\n        - text: 、\n        - code: ’339\n        - text: 三件专利，说明核心温控+传感专利已进入诉讼变现阶段。\n      - paragraph: 启示\n      - list:\n        - listitem: 布局呈\"硬件结构（水路/床垫）→ 传感算法 → 闭环控制 → AI 个性化\"四层递进，后发者需绕开双区水循环与生理信号闭环控制权利要求。\n        - listitem: 如需，我可进一步深挖某件核心专利的权利要求书，或对比 Sleep Number、Chilipad（Sleep.me）的竞对布局。要继续吗？\n      - button:\n      - button:\n      - button:\n      - button:\n      - button:\n    - navigation:\n      - button:\n      - button\n      - button\n      - button\n      - button\n      - button:\n    - button:\n      - text: 最新\n    - textbox:\n      - /placeholder: \"@ 引用对话文件，/ 调用技能与指令，直接说需求...\"\n    - button [expanded]:\n    - button:\n      - generic: 分工协作\n    - button:\n      - text: 引擎：自动\n    - button:\n      - generic: big-pickle\n    - button [disabled]:\n    - button:\n      - generic: 个人空间\n    - button:\n      - generic: 通用\n    - button:\n      - generic: ★\n    - button:\n    - button:\n  - complementary:\n    - separator\n    - button:\n    - tablist:\n      - tab:\n        - generic: 开发工作台\n      - tab:\n        - generic: Diff\n      - button:\n      - tab:\n        - generic: 终端\n      - button:\n      - tab:\n        - generic: 预览\n      - button:\n      - tab:\n        - generic: 产物\n      - button:\n    - button:\n    - button:\n    - region:\n      - button: 概要\n      - generic: Kane\n      - button [expanded]:\n        - heading [level=3]: 进展\n        - generic: 遇到问题 · 1 异常\n      - list:\n        - generic: P1\n        - generic: 补齐上下文\n        - generic: 已完成\n        - generic: P2\n        - generic: 处理线索\n        - generic: 异常\n      - heading [level=3]: 结果回执\n      - generic: 异常\n      - paragraph: 把已完成事项、产物和异常收口到一处，便于快速验收。\n      - paragraph: 错误 stks.freshpatents.com\n      - button [expanded]:\n        - heading [level=3]: 上下文\n      - button: 压缩\n      - button: 1%\n      - button:\n        - generic: 文件\n      - list:\n        - generic: dynamic__platform_read\n        - generic: 已完成\n- region \"Notifications alt+T\"\n- menu \"添加内容\":\n  - menuitem \"上传图片\":\n    - text: 上传图片\n  - menuitem \"项目文件\":\n    - generic: 项目文件\n  - menuitem \"窗口\":\n    - generic: 窗口\n  - separator\n  - menuitem \"命令\":\n    - text: 命令\n  - menuitem \"插件\":\n    - text: 插件\n  - menuitem \"技能\" [expanded] [active]:\n    - text: 技能\n  - menu \"技能\":\n    - textbox \"搜索技能\"\n    - menuitem \"ad-creative When the user wants to generate, iterate, or scale ad creative — headlines, descriptions, primary text, or full ad variations — for any paid advertising platform. Also use when the user mentions 'ad copy variations,' 'ad creative,' 'generate headlines,' 'RSA headlines,' 'bulk ad copy,' 'ad iterations,' 'creative testing,' 'ad performance optimization,' 'write me some ads,' 'Facebook ad copy,' 'Google ad headlines,' 'LinkedIn ad text,' or 'I need more ad variations.' Use this whenever someone needs to produce ad copy at scale or iterate on existing ads.\":\n      - generic: ad-creative\n      - generic: When the user wants to generate, iterate, or scale ad creative — headlines, descriptions, primary text, or full ad variations — for any paid advertising platform. Also use when the user mentions 'ad copy variations,' 'ad creative,' 'generate headlines,' 'RSA headlines,' 'bulk ad copy,' 'ad iterations,' 'creative testing,' 'ad performance optimization,' 'write me some ads,' 'Facebook ad copy,' 'Google ad headlines,' 'LinkedIn ad text,' or 'I need more ad variations.' Use this whenever someone needs to produce ad copy at scale or iterate on existing ads.\n    - menuitem \"agent-generator Generate a complete Octopus Agent from a short natural-language brief. Use when creating, bootstrapping, or refining an Agent from a one-line description, role idea, use case, or persona concept; expands the brief into SOUL, ARM/tool groups, private_skills whitelist, permissions, behavior boundaries, default workflow, and setup_agent-ready configuration.\":\n      - generic: agent-generator\n      - generic: Generate a complete Octopus Agent from a short natural-language brief. Use when creating, bootstrapping, or refining an Agent from a one-line description, role idea, use case, or persona concept; expands the brief into SOUL, ARM/tool groups, private_skills whitelist, permissions, behavior boundaries, default workflow, and setup_agent-ready configuration.\n    - menuitem \"agent-visual-kit Metaskill workflow for generating Octopus Agent character artwork. Use when creating or regenerating Agent portraits, three-view character sheets, transparent-background standees, separate close-up avatars, or visual assets from HUD character profile data; constrains prompt assembly, generation, post-processing, quality checks, and retry reasons.\":\n      - generic: agent-visual-kit\n      - generic: Metaskill workflow for generating Octopus Agent character artwork. Use when creating or regenerating Agent portraits, three-view character sheets, transparent-background standees, separate close-up avatars, or visual assets from HUD character profile data; constrains prompt assembly, generation, post-processing, quality checks, and retry reasons.\n    - menuitem \"agnes-image-generate 使用火山引擎(火山方舟)或 Agnes AI 网关从文字描述生成图像。默认火山 doubao-seedream-5.0-lite（文生图+图生图），未配置火山 key 时自动回退 Agnes agnes-image-2.5-flash。当用户需要生成图片、插画或封面时调用此技能。\":\n      - generic: agnes-image-generate\n      - generic: 使用火山引擎(火山方舟)或 Agnes AI 网关从文字描述生成图像。默认火山 doubao-seedream-5.0-lite（文生图+图生图），未配置火山 key 时自动回退 Agnes agnes-image-2.5-flash。当用户需要生成图片、插画或封面时调用此技能。\n    - menuitem \"agnes-video-generate 使用火山引擎(火山方舟, doubao-seedance-1.5-pro)或 Agnes AI 网关异步提交视频生成任务。默认 wait=true 阻塞到完成并返回 video_url；也可 wait=false 立即返回 task_id，用 agnes-video-poll 查询进度。支持文字到视频、图像到视频(首帧/首尾帧)。\":\n      - generic: agnes-video-generate\n      - generic: 使用火山引擎(火山方舟, doubao-seedance-1.5-pro)或 Agnes AI 网关异步提交视频生成任务。默认 wait=true 阻塞到完成并返回 video_url；也可 wait=false 立即返回 task_id，用 agnes-video-poll 查询进度。支持文字到视频、图像到视频(首帧/首尾帧)。\n    - menuitem \"agnes-video-poll 查询视频生成任务的状态（火山 doubao-seedance 或 Agnes）。配合 agnes-video-generate（wait=false 异步提交）使用——后者返回 task_id 后，模型可在后续轮次用 task_id 调用本技能查看进度或获取 video_url。\":\n      - generic: agnes-video-poll\n      - generic: 查询视频生成任务的状态（火山 doubao-seedance 或 Agnes）。配合 agnes-video-generate（wait=false 异步提交）使用——后者返回 task_id 后，模型可在后续轮次用 task_id 调用本技能查看进度或获取 video_url。\n    - 'menuitem \"analyze_soul_impact Statistical check: did the most recent SOUL.md change help or hurt your turn quality? Compares the average score before vs after the lesson was added. Returns {verdict: improved/regressed/neutral/inconclusive/no_change/no_data, before_avg, after_avg, delta, suggestion}. Run this before considering a `revert_soul`. Zero LLM cost · all heuristic. Args: {window?: int (per side, default 20), drop_threshold?: float (default 0.2)}.\"':\n      - generic: analyze_soul_impact\n      - generic: \"Statistical check: did the most recent SOUL.md change help or hurt your turn quality? Compares the average score before vs after the lesson was added. Returns {verdict: improved/regressed/neutral/inconclusive/no_change/no_data, before_avg, after_avg, delta, suggestion}. Run this before considering a `revert_soul`. Zero LLM cost · all heuristic. Args: {window?: int (per side, default 20), drop_threshold?: float (default 0.2)}.\"\n    - menuitem \"api-and-interface-design Guides stable API and interface design. Use when designing APIs, module boundaries, or any public interface. Use when creating REST or GraphQL endpoints, defining type contracts between modules, or establishing boundaries between frontend and backend.\":\n      - generic: api-and-interface-design\n      - generic: Guides stable API and interface design. Use when designing APIs, module boundaries, or any public interface. Use when creating REST or GraphQL endpoints, defining type contracts between modules, or establishing boundaries between frontend and backend.\n    - menuitem \"api-shape-explorer Generate multiple radically different interface designs for a module using parallel sub-agents. Use when user wants to design an API, explore interface options, compare module shapes, or mentions \\\"design it twice\\\".\":\n      - generic: api-shape-explorer\n      - generic: Generate multiple radically different interface designs for a module using parallel sub-agents. Use when user wants to design an API, explore interface options, compare module shapes, or mentions \"design it twice\".\n    - 'menuitem \"append_text_file 用途: 在文件末尾追加 UTF-8 文本（不存在则创建）；常用于日志、增量记录、向 markdown 续写。 何时不用: 要替换/修改文件中间某段用 edit_file；要整体覆写一个新文件用 write_text_file (overwrite=True)；要在指定位置插入用 edit_file 把上下文一并替换。 关键参数: path (必填); content (必填, 自带换行需自己加 \\\\n); max_bytes (默认 1MB)。 示例: append_text_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"log.txt\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2026-05-29 ok\\\\n\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: append_text_file\n      - generic: \"用途: 在文件末尾追加 UTF-8 文本（不存在则创建）；常用于日志、增量记录、向 markdown 续写。 何时不用: 要替换/修改文件中间某段用 edit_file；要整体覆写一个新文件用 write_text_file (overwrite=True)；要在指定位置插入用 edit_file 把上下文一并替换。 关键参数: path (必填); content (必填, 自带换行需自己加 \\\\n); max_bytes (默认 1MB)。 示例: append_text_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"log.txt\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2026-05-29 ok\\\\n\\\"})\"\n    - menuitem \"apply_candidate_patch Apply a candidate only after inspect_candidate_patch. Pass its opaque inspection_id; never pass a filesystem path. The host revalidates the source, takes all file leases, journals before effects, verifies exact output bytes, and rolls back on failure. A candidate whose artifact contract failed is blocked unless allow_invalid_contract=true is explicitly supplied after diff review.\":\n      - generic: apply_candidate_patch\n      - generic: Apply a candidate only after inspect_candidate_patch. Pass its opaque inspection_id; never pass a filesystem path. The host revalidates the source, takes all file leases, journals before effects, verifies exact output bytes, and rolls back on failure. A candidate whose artifact contract failed is blocked unless allow_invalid_contract=true is explicitly supplied after diff review.\n    - 'menuitem \"apply_skill Apply a learned skill template to produce output matching its shape, for a new user request. The LLM is given the template + style notes and the user''s specific request; reply is markdown matching the template''s structure. Args: {name: skill name (slug), user_request: the specific topic / data to fill in, model?: override}. Use `list_learned_skills` first to see what''s available.\"':\n      - generic: apply_skill\n      - generic: \"Apply a learned skill template to produce output matching its shape, for a new user request. The LLM is given the template + style notes and the user's specific request; reply is markdown matching the template's structure. Args: {name: skill name (slug), user_request: the specific topic / data to fill in, model?: override}. Use `list_learned_skills` first to see what's available.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"ask_user_question 用途: 暂停并以结构化卡片向用户提一个 2-6 选项的问题, 仅用于【多个并列方案的产品决策】——选项之间是真正的取舍, 且用户最有资格拍板。例: 用哪个数据库、用哪个框架、走哪种部署方式。 何时不用 (重要): - 开放任务的方向/范围澄清 (如 ''你想调研哪方面''、''聚焦哪个领域'') ——不要用本工具反问。先按最合理的理解做一轮, 并在开头一句话亮明假设 (''我按 X 理解, 不对请说''), 让用户在看到产出后纠偏, 而不是上来就问。 - 单一文件改动、信息查询: 用 web_search / read_file。 - yes/no 工具批准: 用 request_approval。 关键参数: question (字符串, 非空); options (2-6 字符串列表, 每项是一个互斥的具体方案); allow_other (默认 True, 允许用户填自定义答案)。 示例: ask_user_question({\\\"question\\\":\\\"用哪个数据库?\\\",\\\"options\\\":[\\\"PostgreSQL\\\",\\\"SQLite\\\",\\\"MySQL\\\"]})\"':\n      - generic: ask_user_question\n      - generic: \"用途: 暂停并以结构化卡片向用户提一个 2-6 选项的问题, 仅用于【多个并列方案的产品决策】——选项之间是真正的取舍, 且用户最有资格拍板。例: 用哪个数据库、用哪个框架、走哪种部署方式。 何时不用 (重要): - 开放任务的方向/范围澄清 (如 '你想调研哪方面'、'聚焦哪个领域') ——不要用本工具反问。先按最合理的理解做一轮, 并在开头一句话亮明假设 ('我按 X 理解, 不对请说'), 让用户在看到产出后纠偏, 而不是上来就问。 - 单一文件改动、信息查询: 用 web_search / read_file。 - yes/no 工具批准: 用 request_approval。 关键参数: question (字符串, 非空); options (2-6 字符串列表, 每项是一个互斥的具体方案); allow_other (默认 True, 允许用户填自定义答案)。 示例: ask_user_question({\\\"question\\\":\\\"用哪个数据库?\\\",\\\"options\\\":[\\\"PostgreSQL\\\",\\\"SQLite\\\",\\\"MySQL\\\"]})\"\n    - menuitem \"audit-xls Audit a spreadsheet for formula accuracy, errors, and common mistakes. Scopes to a selected range, a single sheet, or the entire model (including financial-model integrity checks like BS balance, cash tie-out, and logic sanity). Triggers on \\\"audit this sheet\\\", \\\"check my formulas\\\", \\\"find formula errors\\\", \\\"QA this spreadsheet\\\", \\\"sanity check this\\\", \\\"debug model\\\", \\\"model check\\\", \\\"model won't balance\\\", \\\"something's off in my model\\\", \\\"model review\\\".\":\n      - generic: audit-xls\n      - generic: Audit a spreadsheet for formula accuracy, errors, and common mistakes. Scopes to a selected range, a single sheet, or the entire model (including financial-model integrity checks like BS balance, cash tie-out, and logic sanity). Triggers on \"audit this sheet\", \"check my formulas\", \"find formula errors\", \"QA this spreadsheet\", \"sanity check this\", \"debug model\", \"model check\", \"model won't balance\", \"something's off in my model\", \"model review\".\n    - 'menuitem \"auto_regression_check Anti-self-harm guard: if the most recent SOUL.md change is hurting your scores (after_n ≥ 5 samples · delta < -threshold), automatically roll back via `revert_soul`. This is the safety counterpart to `deep_evolve(dry_run=False)`: register a governed candidate, this path verifies it actually helped. Zero LLM cost · defaults dry_run=False so it really reverts when triggered. Returns {action: reverted/would_revert/no_action, analysis, revert_result}. Args: {window?: int (default 20), drop_threshold?: float (default 0.2), min_samples?: int (default 5), dry_run?: bool (default False · set True to only report without reverting)}.\"':\n      - generic: auto_regression_check\n      - generic: \"Anti-self-harm guard: if the most recent SOUL.md change is hurting your scores (after_n ≥ 5 samples · delta < -threshold), automatically roll back via `revert_soul`. This is the safety counterpart to `deep_evolve(dry_run=False)`: register a governed candidate, this path verifies it actually helped. Zero LLM cost · defaults dry_run=False so it really reverts when triggered. Returns {action: reverted/would_revert/no_action, analysis, revert_result}. Args: {window?: int (default 20), drop_threshold?: float (default 0.2), min_samples?: int (default 5), dry_run?: bool (default False · set True to only report without reverting)}.\"\n    - menuitem \"auto-stat-test 自动执行统计检验，根据数据特征（组数、正态性、配对设计）智能选择 t 检验、卡方检验、ANOVA、Mann-Whitney U 等合适方法，并输出包含 p 值、效应量和通俗中文解读的完整报告。当用户需要进行假设检验、组间比较、显著性分析，或提及 t 检验、卡方、方差分析、p 值、配对检验、非参数检验等关键词时触发。\":\n      - generic: auto-stat-test\n      - generic: 自动执行统计检验，根据数据特征（组数、正态性、配对设计）智能选择 t 检验、卡方检验、ANOVA、Mann-Whitney U 等合适方法，并输出包含 p 值、效应量和通俗中文解读的完整报告。当用户需要进行假设检验、组间比较、显著性分析，或提及 t 检验、卡方、方差分析、p 值、配对检验、非参数检验等关键词时触发。\n    - menuitem \"backend-building Backend building that grafts tRPC + Drizzle ORM + Hono onto an existing webapp-building frontend. Supports incremental features (db, auth). Use when the user needs a backend, API, database, server, authentication, or wants to add tRPC/Drizzle to their webapp-building project. Requires webapp-building first.\":\n      - generic: backend-building\n      - generic: Backend building that grafts tRPC + Drizzle ORM + Hono onto an existing webapp-building frontend. Supports incremental features (db, auth). Use when the user needs a backend, API, database, server, authentication, or wants to add tRPC/Drizzle to their webapp-building project. Requires webapp-building first.\n    - 'menuitem \"background_exec Start a LOCAL long-running command in the background and return immediately with a task_id. Use for dev servers, watchers, docker compose, and long tests. Poll with `read_background_output`; stop with `kill_background_exec`.\"':\n      - generic: background_exec\n      - generic: \"Start a LOCAL long-running command in the background and return immediately with a task_id. Use for dev servers, watchers, docker compose, and long tests. Poll with `read_background_output`; stop with `kill_background_exec`.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"bb_claim Claim a blackboard slot for the current agent. Once claimed, only the claiming agent can write that key — siblings can still read it. Use to avoid two parallel sub-agents stomping each other''s coordination slot (e.g. `bb_claim(key=''owner'')`). Args: {key: string}.\"':\n      - generic: bb_claim\n      - generic: \"Claim a blackboard slot for the current agent. Once claimed, only the claiming agent can write that key — siblings can still read it. Use to avoid two parallel sub-agents stomping each other's coordination slot (e.g. `bb_claim(key='owner')`). Args: {key: string}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"bb_keys List all keys currently on the shared blackboard. Useful when you don''t know what your concurrent siblings have written yet — call `bb_keys()` first, then `bb_read(k)` on the interesting ones. Returns {ok, keys, count}.\"':\n      - generic: bb_keys\n      - generic: \"List all keys currently on the shared blackboard. Useful when you don't know what your concurrent siblings have written yet — call `bb_keys()` first, then `bb_read(k)` on the interesting ones. Returns {ok, keys, count}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"bb_pin Seal a blackboard key as an immutable snapshot. After pinning, no further writes to that key are accepted. Use to lock a final decision so parallel workers can''t overwrite it. Args: {key: string}.\"':\n      - generic: bb_pin\n      - generic: \"Seal a blackboard key as an immutable snapshot. After pinning, no further writes to that key are accepted. Use to lock a final decision so parallel workers can't overwrite it. Args: {key: string}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"bb_read Read a value from the shared blackboard. Returns {ok, found, key, value}. `found=False` means no entry exists for that key yet. Use this to check what other concurrent sub-agents (or the lead) have written. Args: {key: string}.\"':\n      - generic: bb_read\n      - generic: \"Read a value from the shared blackboard. Returns {ok, found, key, value}. `found=False` means no entry exists for that key yet. Use this to check what other concurrent sub-agents (or the lead) have written. Args: {key: string}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"bb_save Persist a LARGE value as a file artifact and return a reference (path + hash). Use this instead of bb_write when the payload is bigger than a small coordination fact — the blackboard is for tiny facts, big payloads live in files. Args: {key: string, value: any JSON-serializable}.\"':\n      - generic: bb_save\n      - generic: \"Persist a LARGE value as a file artifact and return a reference (path + hash). Use this instead of bb_write when the payload is bigger than a small coordination fact — the blackboard is for tiny facts, big payloads live in files. Args: {key: string, value: any JSON-serializable}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"bb_write Write a value to the shared blackboard. The blackboard is an in-memory key/value store scoped to the current turn — lead agent + all concurrent sub-agents share it. Use it to pass findings between parallel workers (e.g. `bb_write(key=''competitor_a'', value={...})`). Args: {key: string, value: any JSON-serializable}. DON''T use for things that should persist across turns — use `remember` for that.\"':\n      - generic: bb_write\n      - generic: \"Write a value to the shared blackboard. The blackboard is an in-memory key/value store scoped to the current turn — lead agent + all concurrent sub-agents share it. Use it to pass findings between parallel workers (e.g. `bb_write(key='competitor_a', value={...})`). Args: {key: string, value: any JSON-serializable}. DON'T use for things that should persist across turns — use `remember` for that.\"\n    - menuitem \"brand-name-forge A systematic brand naming workshop that generates 8 distinct name candidates using classic methods like portmanteau and metaphor, each with meaning, rationale, and domain suggestions. Triggered when a user needs to name a product, service, or company, or asks for brand name ideas, brainstorming, or naming help.\":\n      - generic: brand-name-forge\n      - generic: A systematic brand naming workshop that generates 8 distinct name candidates using classic methods like portmanteau and metaphor, each with meaning, rationale, and domain suggestions. Triggered when a user needs to name a product, service, or company, or asks for brand name ideas, brainstorming, or naming help.\n    - menuitem \"break-trace Root-cause a reconciliation break to its source transaction or posting — follow the audit trail from the break row back to the originating entry on each side and state what differs and why. Use after gl-recon has classified a break.\":\n      - generic: break-trace\n      - generic: Root-cause a reconciliation break to its source transaction or posting — follow the audit trail from the break row back to the originating entry on each side and state what differs and why. Use after gl-recon has classified a break.\n    - menuitem \"browse Automate browser interactions via CLI commands to navigate web pages, extract data, take screenshots, fill forms, and interact with web apps. Supports remote sessions with CAPTCHA solving and anti-bot stealth for scraping protected sites. Trigger when the user asks to browse websites, scrape data, or automate clicks on any page.\":\n      - generic: browse\n      - generic: Automate browser interactions via CLI commands to navigate web pages, extract data, take screenshots, fill forms, and interact with web apps. Supports remote sessions with CAPTCHA solving and anti-bot stealth for scraping protected sites. Trigger when the user asks to browse websites, scrape data, or automate clicks on any page.\n    - menuitem \"browser_click Click a CSS selector on the current persistent page; url is optional and navigates first when supplied.\":\n      - generic: browser_click\n      - generic: Click a CSS selector on the current persistent page; url is optional and navigates first when supplied.\n    - menuitem \"browser_extract Extract CSS matches (text or attr). Pass url to navigate, or omit it to use the current persistent agent browser page.\":\n      - generic: browser_extract\n      - generic: Extract CSS matches (text or attr). Pass url to navigate, or omit it to use the current persistent agent browser page.\n    - menuitem \"browser_find Navigate to a page and find text, returning match snippets.\":\n      - generic: browser_find\n      - generic: Navigate to a page and find text, returning match snippets.\n    - menuitem \"browser_get Read rendered title, body text, and child-frame text. Pass url to navigate first, or omit url to read the current persistent agent browser page; use wait_ms before reading delayed UI or iframe confirmations.\":\n      - generic: browser_get\n      - generic: Read rendered title, body text, and child-frame text. Pass url to navigate first, or omit url to read the current persistent agent browser page; use wait_ms before reading delayed UI or iframe confirmations.\n    - menuitem \"browser_navigate Navigate the persistent agent browser page to a URL and return final URL + status.\":\n      - generic: browser_navigate\n      - generic: Navigate the persistent agent browser page to a URL and return final URL + status.\n    - menuitem \"browser_screenshot Navigate and save a page screenshot (path_guard enforced).\":\n      - generic: browser_screenshot\n      - generic: Navigate and save a page screenshot (path_guard enforced).\n    - menuitem \"browser_scroll Navigate and scroll to element or Y coordinate.\":\n      - generic: browser_scroll\n      - generic: Navigate and scroll to element or Y coordinate.\n    - 'menuitem \"browser_state Return persistent browser state (optionally navigate with url): title, URL, viewport, scroll, child-frame text, and visible links/buttons/inputs/headings.\"':\n      - generic: browser_state\n      - generic: \"Return persistent browser state (optionally navigate with url): title, URL, viewport, scroll, child-frame text, and visible links/buttons/inputs/headings.\"\n    - menuitem \"browser_type Fill an input/contenteditable or choose a native select option by visible label/value on the current persistent page; url is optional and navigates first when supplied. Pass content as text (value and option_label are also accepted aliases).\":\n      - generic: browser_type\n      - generic: Fill an input/contenteditable or choose a native select option by visible label/value on the current persistent page; url is optional and navigates first when supplied. Pass content as text (value and option_label are also accepted aliases).\n    - menuitem \"browser_upload Upload a workspace file into a CSS-selected file input on the current persistent page. Pass selector and path; url is optional after navigation.\":\n      - generic: browser_upload\n      - generic: Upload a workspace file into a CSS-selected file input on the current persistent page. Pass selector and path; url is optional after navigation.\n    - menuitem \"browser_wait Wait on the current persistent page for a CSS selector state; url is optional.\":\n      - generic: browser_wait\n      - generic: Wait on the current persistent page for a CSS selector state; url is optional.\n    - menuitem \"browser-testing-with-devtools Tests in real browsers. Use when building or debugging anything that runs in a browser. Use when you need to inspect the DOM, capture console errors, analyze network requests, profile performance, or verify visual output with real runtime data via Chrome DevTools MCP.\":\n      - generic: browser-testing-with-devtools\n      - generic: Tests in real browsers. Use when building or debugging anything that runs in a browser. Use when you need to inspect the DOM, capture console errors, analyze network requests, profile performance, or verify visual output with real runtime data via Chrome DevTools MCP.\n    - menuitem \"business-plan-ppt 创建专业精美的投资路演PPT和商业计划书，风格参照中国创业公司融资路演材料，默认输出18页、白色背景搭配藏青色点缀的PPTX格式，也可导出PDF，支持中英文内容。当用户需要为投资人制作路演PPT、撰写商业计划书或融资方案、生成包含市场分析和财务预测的公司概览幻灯片，或提及创业融资/投资备忘录演示文稿时触发。\":\n      - generic: business-plan-ppt\n      - generic: 创建专业精美的投资路演PPT和商业计划书，风格参照中国创业公司融资路演材料，默认输出18页、白色背景搭配藏青色点缀的PPTX格式，也可导出PDF，支持中英文内容。当用户需要为投资人制作路演PPT、撰写商业计划书或融资方案、生成包含市场分析和财务预测的公司概览幻灯片，或提及创业融资/投资备忘录演示文稿时触发。\n    - menuitem:\n      - generic: call_agent\n      - generic: \"Spawn an isolated specialist subagent for one focused subtask. The subagent runs in its own context window with its own tools, runs ONE turn, returns a single summary string back to you. This tool exists and works · the guidance below is about WHEN to use it, not whether you have it. Frequency: this is an EXCEPTION tool in normal chat/code turns, not a default reflex. In explicit `swarm` mode it may be used as part of a dynamic orchestration plan when the task is large enough. Most tasks lead handles itself. Hard cap is 1 call per turn — if you need delegation again on the same turn, the second call returns an error · do that work yourself. Use it when ALL three are true: 1. The subtask falls inside an advertised specialist role. 2. The lead's general competence is genuinely insufficient — you've thought about it for at least one turn first. 3. You haven't already used `call_agent` this turn. Skip delegation (do it yourself with normal tools) for: - Anything you can finish in ≤ 2 more turns. - Code work touching ≤ 3 files (read / edit / debug). - Web research / fact lookup → use `web_search`. - 'I don't know how to start' reflex → just start. - Asking the user a clarifying question → reply directly. When the user asks for MULTIPLE delegations in one turn: pick the single most-specialist task and delegate that, then handle the rest yourself in the same turn. Tell the user what you split. Don't refuse the whole request — delegate one, do the others. Args: {agent_id: string (one of the names below), prompt: string (focused brief, written like a user message), skills?/tools?: list of concrete skill names, skill_pack(s)?: one or more of research/web/browser/files/code/review/write/memory/shell, plugins?: plugin or package hints, output_schema?: a JSON Schema object — pass it when you need the subagent's answer as a validated JSON object you can parse (returned under `parsed`), e.g. {\\\"type\\\":\\\"object\\\",\\\"properties\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\"}},\\\"required\\\":[\\\"verdict\\\"]}}. Use skill packs when the subtask needs tools beyond the role's default allowlist. For a file handoff, pass input_files and output_files as file path lists. Use isolate=true for a candidate code change in a host-created worktree. It includes current uncommitted project files and returns a durable patch for verification and application. The host snapshots inputs, verifies required output files, and returns artifacts with hashes and producer identity. A failed file handoff is not retried automatically; inspect its result before redispatching. Advertised specialist roles: - architect: Reasons about system design trade-offs · inherits both conversation and memory so it has full project context. - debugger: Traces the root cause of a reported bug · inherits the caller's conversation to understand the observed symptom. - explorer: Fast navigation of the repo to answer structural questions like 'where is X defined?' · 'who calls Y?' - researcher: Deep-dives a single topic using web search + URL fetch. Does NOT inherit memory by default · researches in a vacuum so prior beliefs don't color the findings. - reviewer: Scans a code change for bugs, security holes, performance issues, and maintainability smells. Shares main agent's conversation context so it can review what ... - security-review: Scans a change for security vulnerabilities · XSS / SQLi / auth bypass / secrets / path traversal / deserialization.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"call_agent_background Start a subagent in the background and return a job id immediately. The child runs asynchronously; when it settles, the parent is notified in-session with the outcome. Collect the result with job_output (set wait: true only when you are genuinely blocked on it) and stop it with job_kill when it stops mattering. Do not busy-poll or sleep on a background job — keep working on independent steps and do not duplicate a running job''s work. Arguments: agent_id (string, required — the subagent role/agent id), prompt (string, required — the child''s task), label (string, optional — one-line display label), timeout_s (number, optional — wall-clock cap in seconds, default 600).\"':\n      - generic: call_agent_background\n      - generic: \"Start a subagent in the background and return a job id immediately. The child runs asynchronously; when it settles, the parent is notified in-session with the outcome. Collect the result with job_output (set wait: true only when you are genuinely blocked on it) and stop it with job_kill when it stops mattering. Do not busy-poll or sleep on a background job — keep working on independent steps and do not duplicate a running job's work. Arguments: agent_id (string, required — the subagent role/agent id), prompt (string, required — the child's task), label (string, optional — one-line display label), timeout_s (number, optional — wall-clock cap in seconds, default 600).\"\n    - menuitem:\n      - generic: call_agent_graph\n      - generic: \"Run a DAG of subagents where one lane CONSUMES another lane's output. Declare each node's `depends_on`; independent nodes run concurrently and the runtime derives the execution order. Use it when call_agent_parallel is not enough because a later step needs an earlier step's result: - two investigations in parallel, then one node that reconciles both; - find → verify → write-up, where each stage reads the last; - a diamond: split into lanes, then fold back into one answer. A node prompt may reference an upstream output: {node_id.output} — that node's full reply text {node_id.output.field} — a field, when that node used output_schema The substitution happens SERVER-SIDE, so upstream text never passes through your context — that is the point of using a graph instead of running lanes yourself and pasting results into the next prompt. Prefer call_agent_parallel when lanes are independent (cheaper, one layer). Prefer run_pipeline when many ITEMS each need the same stage chain. Use this when the TOPOLOGY itself has a join. Args: {nodes: list[{id: str, prompt: str, depends_on?: list[str], agent_id?: str, output_schema?: object, isolate?: bool, when?: object}] (up to 12), default_agent_id?: str (default researcher), timeout_s?: int (per-subagent, default 900), resume_token?: str (from a previous run's return)}. `isolate: true` gives that node its own git worktree — set it on nodes that EDIT FILES so concurrent writers in the same layer cannot collide. The node's diff comes back for review; nothing is auto-merged. Returns: {ok, nodes:{id:{id, agent_id, output, ok, error?, skipped?}}, order:[[id,...],...] (execution layers), terminal:[str] (leaf outputs), layers_run, success_count, failure_count, total}. Cycles and unknown depends_on are rejected before any spawn. A node whose upstream failed is skipped and reported, not run with an unresolved placeholder. Conditional branches: `when` is a bounded data-only expression over explicit dependency output, e.g. `{ref:'judge.output.approved', op:'eq', value:true}`. Operators: eq/ne/truthy/falsy/in/not_in/contains/gt/gte/lt/lte; combine with `all`, `any`, or `not`. A false branch is skipped without spending a spawn. Arbitrary code, back-edges and unbounded loops are rejected. Budget: one graph costs ONE against the 5/turn delegation cap; per-node spawns are charged against the internal spawn budget. Resume: pass the returned `resume_token` back to re-run the same graph without respawning completed nodes - unchanged nodes replay their recorded result (0 spawns), a node whose prompt/role/schema changed respawns, and failed or empty nodes always re-run. The token is in-memory only (not valid across process restarts) and an unknown token is an error, not a cold run.\"\n    - menuitem:\n      - generic: call_agent_parallel\n      - generic: \"Spawn N sub-agents CONCURRENTLY (Kimi-style swarm) for tasks that decompose cleanly into independent sub-tasks each needing a specialist. All siblings + lead share a turn-scoped blackboard (bb_read / bb_write / bb_keys) so they can exchange partial findings. Availability: this is a real parallel delegation tool in ordinary Agent/ReAct mode as well as explicit swarm mode. In Agent mode, use it when multiple independent lanes would materially improve speed or quality; the lead remains responsible for synthesis and final delivery. Use it when: - The task is genuinely parallel (research lanes, file areas, vendor comparisons, review lanes), AND - Each sub-task fits an advertised specialist role, AND - The lead can integrate the returned summaries into a final deliverable in the same turn. Skip if: - Sub-tasks are sequential (each depends on previous output) — use serial reasoning instead. - You'd just be parallelizing trivial work — overhead > gain. - A single web_search/read_file pass is enough. Swarm workflow hint: update todo_write first, assign independent roles dynamically, ask workers to bb_write compact findings under clear keys, then bb_keys/bb_read, synthesize, verify/cross-check, and produce the final answer or file deliverable. Do NOT stop after the parallel call with only raw worker logs. Honesty contract: if the returned envelope has ``partial=True`` or ``failed > 0``, your final answer MUST include a brief run-status line such as \\\"Subagent status: 3/5 succeeded; 2 failed\\\" and MUST not say that all lanes completed. Name the failed lanes from ``failures[].task_label`` / ``failures[].agent_id`` and either disclose the gap or explicitly describe how you filled it yourself. Budget (2026-06 smart-budget): Each spec counts independently. First-time failures are FREE (you can fix and retry). Repeat failures (same agent + same prompt) count. Absolute cap: 5 delegations/turn. Wall-clock = max(per-agent time), not sum. Args: {specs: list[{agent_id: string, prompt: string, task_id?: string, objective?: string, inputs?: list|string, deliverable?: string, dependencies?: list[string], acceptance_criteria?: list[string]|string, skills?/tools?: list of concrete skill names, skill_pack(s)?: research/web/browser/files/code/review/write/memory/shell, plugins?: plugin/package hints, input_files?: list[string], output_files?: list[string], isolate?: bool}], timeout_s?: int (per-agent, default 900), completion_policy?: all|first_completed|first_success|quorum (default all), quorum?: int (strict majority by default)}. Use first_success for redundant racers and quorum when enough independent evidence should settle the batch; unused lanes are cooperatively cancelled to stop token spend. Use the canonical keys `agent_id` and `prompt`. Legacy `role` and `goal` are accepted for compatibility, but do not prefer them in new calls. For coordinated deliverables, include task_id, objective, deliverable, dependencies, and acceptance_criteria on every spec. These fields are persisted as the recoverable task graph; do not hide them only inside prompt. `isolate: true` runs that ONE spec inside its own git worktree, so its writes cannot collide with a sibling's. Set it on every lane that EDITS FILES when more than one lane writes — parallel writes to a shared checkout corrupt each other. Read-only lanes should leave it off (a worktree costs a checkout). The host snapshots current working files, including uncommitted changes, and returns a durable `worktree.patch` reference with a `diff` preview. Changes require verification and explicit application to the project. The worktree lives until the actual child stops; failed or cancelled attempts preserve partial patches and do not auto-retry. The host chooses the directory within the task's approved output scope. Returns: {ok, successes:[{role, agent_id, output, files_touched, diff?, worktree?, isolated?, artifacts?, artifact_handoff?}], failures:[{role, agent_id, error, error_type}], partial, total, success_count, completion_policy, completion_target, policy_satisfied, cancelled_count, notes:[...], plus legacy keys (results, count, succeeded, failed, outputs)}. ``ok=False`` only when zero workers succeed — partial failures still return ok=True with the surviving outputs and a [partial-degradation] note in ``notes`` so you can synthesise from what came back. Available specialist roles (same as call_agent): - architect: Reasons about system design trade-offs · inherits both conversation and memory so it has full project context. - debugger: Traces the root cause of a reported bug · inherits the caller's conversation to understand the observed symptom. - explorer: Fast navigation of the repo to answer structural questions like 'where is X defined?' · 'who calls Y?' - researcher: Deep-dives a single topic using web search + URL fetch. Does NOT inherit memory by default · researches in a vacuum so prior beliefs don't color the findings. - reviewer: Scans a code change for bugs, security holes, performance issues, and maintainability smells. Shares main agent's conversation context so it can review what ... - security-review: Scans a change for security vulnerabilities · XSS / SQLi / auth bypass / secrets / path traversal / deserialization.\"\n    - menuitem:\n      - generic: call_agent_vote\n      - generic: \"Verification gate — spawn N INDEPENDENT voters on the SAME question and tally a MAJORITY verdict (with confidence + dissent). This is the adversarial-verify / judge-panel pattern: confirm or refute a claim with independent judgment instead of trusting one agent. Use it for decisions that matter: 'is this bug real?', 'does this patch actually fix it?', 'is this answer correct?', 'which option is safer: A or B?'. A natural pairing is call_agent_parallel (gather candidate answers) → call_agent_vote (adjudicate them). Each voter runs in its own context and must emit `VERDICT: <choice>` then `REASON: <one line>`. Unparseable replies count as abstentions; a split returns verdict=null with tie=true (no decision — you break it or escalate). Args: {question: string (the claim / question to judge), n?: int 2-5 voters (default 3 · odd avoids ties), choices?: list[string] a fixed ballot e.g. [\\\"yes\\\",\\\"no\\\"] (omit for a free-form verdict), agent_id?: voter role (default reviewer), timeout_s?: int}. Returns: {ok, verdict (null on tie / no-verdict), confidence (0-1), unanimous, tie, tie_between, tally:{choice:count}, votes:[{verdict, reason, codename, abstained}], votes_cast, abstentions, note, honesty_warning}. Budget: each voter is one delegation against the 5/turn cap, so a 3-voter vote uses 3. Reserve it for decisions worth the spend.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"cancel_scheduled_task Remove a scheduled task by id. Returns {ok, task_id, deleted} on success, or {ok: false, error, error_type: ''not_found''} if no task with that id exists.\"':\n      - generic: cancel_scheduled_task\n      - generic: \"Remove a scheduled task by id. Returns {ok, task_id, deleted} on success, or {ok: false, error, error_type: 'not_found'} if no task with that id exists.\"\n    - menuitem \"chart-image Generate publication-quality PNG chart images from data, supporting line, bar, area, candlestick, pie, and heatmap charts. Triggers when the user asks to visualize data, create a graph, plot a time series, or generate a chart for a report, alert, or dashboard. Runs as a lightweight, headless Node.js process without a browser.\":\n      - generic: chart-image\n      - generic: Generate publication-quality PNG chart images from data, supporting line, bar, area, candlestick, pie, and heatmap charts. Triggers when the user asks to visualize data, create a graph, plot a time series, or generate a chart for a report, alert, or dashboard. Runs as a lightweight, headless Node.js process without a browser.\n    - menuitem \"client-review Prepare for client review meetings with portfolio performance summary, allocation analysis, talking points, and action items. Pulls together account data into a concise meeting-ready format. Use before quarterly reviews, annual checkups, or ad-hoc client meetings. Triggers on \\\"client review\\\", \\\"meeting prep for [client]\\\", \\\"quarterly review\\\", \\\"prep for [client name]\\\", or \\\"client meeting\\\".\":\n      - generic: client-review\n      - generic: Prepare for client review meetings with portfolio performance summary, allocation analysis, talking points, and action items. Pulls together account data into a concise meeting-ready format. Use before quarterly reviews, annual checkups, or ad-hoc client meetings. Triggers on \"client review\", \"meeting prep for [client]\", \"quarterly review\", \"prep for [client name]\", or \"client meeting\".\n    - menuitem \"clip_studio.project_get 读取本地 AI 剪辑工坊项目。参数 project_id 必填；view 可选 summary/tracks/clips/full，默认 clips。返回轨道、片段、字幕与时长。\":\n      - generic: clip_studio.project_get\n      - generic: 读取本地 AI 剪辑工坊项目。参数 project_id 必填；view 可选 summary/tracks/clips/full，默认 clips。返回轨道、片段、字幕与时长。\n    - menuitem \"cn-finance-data 通过 Tushare Pro 获取中国金融市场数据，覆盖 A 股、港股、美股、基金、期货、债券等 220+ 个数据接口，可查询股票行情、财务报表、指数成分、GDP/CPI 等宏观经济指标。当用户请求金融数据查询、股票历史行情、财务指标分析、宏观数据获取，或提及 Tushare、数据接口、量化数据源等关键词时触发。\":\n      - generic: cn-finance-data\n      - generic: 通过 Tushare Pro 获取中国金融市场数据，覆盖 A 股、港股、美股、基金、期货、债券等 220+ 个数据接口，可查询股票行情、财务报表、指数成分、GDP/CPI 等宏观经济指标。当用户请求金融数据查询、股票历史行情、财务指标分析、宏观数据获取，或提及 Tushare、数据接口、量化数据源等关键词时触发。\n    - 'menuitem \"code_analyze 解析代码文件的 AST 结构。返回 functions/classes/imports/call_graph。支持 Python（精确 AST）和 JS/TS/Go/Rust/Java（正则 fallback）。Args: {path: string} 或 {content: string, language?: string}。用于理解代码结构、查找函数定义、分析依赖关系。\"':\n      - generic: code_analyze\n      - generic: \"解析代码文件的 AST 结构。返回 functions/classes/imports/call_graph。支持 Python（精确 AST）和 JS/TS/Go/Rust/Java（正则 fallback）。Args: {path: string} 或 {content: string, language?: string}。用于理解代码结构、查找函数定义、分析依赖关系。\"\n    - 'menuitem \"code_dependency_graph 分析 Python 项目的文件间 import 依赖图。返回 nodes（文件）和 edges（import 关系），可用于理解项目结构。Args: {directory?: string, package?: string}。\"':\n      - generic: code_dependency_graph\n      - generic: \"分析 Python 项目的文件间 import 依赖图。返回 nodes（文件）和 edges（import 关系），可用于理解项目结构。Args: {directory?: string, package?: string}。\"\n    - 'menuitem \"code_edit_diff Diff 级代码编辑。两种模式：(1) search/replace 精确文本替换 Args: {path, search, replace}；(2) unified diff 应用 Args: {path, diff}。比整文件覆写更安全精确。\"':\n      - generic: code_edit_diff\n      - generic: \"Diff 级代码编辑。两种模式：(1) search/replace 精确文本替换 Args: {path, search, replace}；(2) unified diff 应用 Args: {path, diff}。比整文件覆写更安全精确。\"\n    - 'menuitem \"code_find_symbol 跨文件查找符号定义位置。精确定位函数/类/变量在哪个文件哪一行定义。Args: {symbol: string, directory?: string}。用于''跳转到定义''、''查找所有引用''等代码导航场景。\"':\n      - generic: code_find_symbol\n      - generic: \"跨文件查找符号定义位置。精确定位函数/类/变量在哪个文件哪一行定义。Args: {symbol: string, directory?: string}。用于'跳转到定义'、'查找所有引用'等代码导航场景。\"\n    - 'menuitem \"code_search 代码搜索。两种模式：(1) 默认 mode=''regex'' — 语义/embedding 搜索，Args: {query: string, directory?: string, top_k?: int}。首次调用会索引目录，后续复用。无 sentence-transformers 时退化为文本搜索。(2) mode=''ast'' — tree-sitter 结构化搜索，Args: {mode:''ast'', query_type:''function_calls''|''function_definitions''|''class_definitions''|''imports'', target_name: string, root?: string, glob?: string}. 跳过注释/字符串中的伪命中。\"':\n      - generic: code_search\n      - generic: \"代码搜索。两种模式：(1) 默认 mode='regex' — 语义/embedding 搜索，Args: {query: string, directory?: string, top_k?: int}。首次调用会索引目录，后续复用。无 sentence-transformers 时退化为文本搜索。(2) mode='ast' — tree-sitter 结构化搜索，Args: {mode:'ast', query_type:'function_calls'|'function_definitions'|'class_definitions'|'imports', target_name: string, root?: string, glob?: string}. 跳过注释/字符串中的伪命中。\"\n    - menuitem \"code-arch-optimizer 探索代码库，识别架构摩擦点，并通过“加深浅模块”来提升可测试性，最终输出包含多种接口设计方案的详细重构建议与GitHub Issue RFC。当用户希望改进架构、寻找重构机会、合并紧耦合模块，或让代码库更易于AI导航和理解时触发。\":\n      - generic: code-arch-optimizer\n      - generic: 探索代码库，识别架构摩擦点，并通过“加深浅模块”来提升可测试性，最终输出包含多种接口设计方案的详细重构建议与GitHub Issue RFC。当用户希望改进架构、寻找重构机会、合并紧耦合模块，或让代码库更易于AI导航和理解时触发。\n    - menuitem \"code-mentor Comprehensive AI programming tutor offering interactive lessons, code reviews, debugging help, algorithm practice, and project guidance for Python and JavaScript. Triggers when users ask to learn a language, debug code, review their work, practice algorithms, prepare for interviews, or build a project.\":\n      - generic: code-mentor\n      - generic: Comprehensive AI programming tutor offering interactive lessons, code reviews, debugging help, algorithm practice, and project guidance for Python and JavaScript. Triggers when users ask to learn a language, debug code, review their work, practice algorithms, prepare for interviews, or build a project.\n    - menuitem \"code-quality 代码质量技能，包含代码审查、重构、性能优化、最佳实践检查。在代码审查或重构时调用。\":\n      - generic: code-quality\n      - generic: 代码质量技能，包含代码审查、重构、性能优化、最佳实践检查。在代码审查或重构时调用。\n    - 'menuitem \"code-vuln-audit Scan code for security issues: dependency vulnerabilities (npm/pip audit), secret leaks (regex and entropy analysis), and OWASP anti-patterns like SQL injection, XSS, or command injection. Use when the user mentions security scans, vulnerability detection, secret leaks, API keys, OWASP, npm audit, pip-audit, hardcoded passwords, or code security checks.\"':\n      - generic: code-vuln-audit\n      - generic: \"Scan code for security issues: dependency vulnerabilities (npm/pip audit), secret leaks (regex and entropy analysis), and OWASP anti-patterns like SQL injection, XSS, or command injection. Use when the user mentions security scans, vulnerability detection, secret leaks, API keys, OWASP, npm audit, pip-audit, hardcoded passwords, or code security checks.\"\n    - menuitem \"comfyui_bridge.status 探测本机 ComfyUI 是否在线并返回 system_stats。不访问远程地址。\":\n      - generic: comfyui_bridge.status\n      - generic: 探测本机 ComfyUI 是否在线并返回 system_stats。不访问远程地址。\n    - menuitem \"competitive-seo-intel 深入分析竞争对手的SEO与GEO策略，涵盖关键词排名、内容打法、外链画像、技术SEO评估及AI引用模式，识别超越对手的市场机会，并提供竞品分析模板、战斗卡片等参考。当用户询问“分析竞品SEO”、“竞争对手为什么排名更高”、“竞品关键词和外链分析”或“内容策略对比”时触发。如需专项分析，可使用content-gap-analysis进行内容差距分析，或使用backlink-analyzer进行外链深度分析。\":\n      - generic: competitive-seo-intel\n      - generic: 深入分析竞争对手的SEO与GEO策略，涵盖关键词排名、内容打法、外链画像、技术SEO评估及AI引用模式，识别超越对手的市场机会，并提供竞品分析模板、战斗卡片等参考。当用户询问“分析竞品SEO”、“竞争对手为什么排名更高”、“竞品关键词和外链分析”或“内容策略对比”时触发。如需专项分析，可使用content-gap-analysis进行内容差距分析，或使用backlink-analyzer进行外链深度分析。\n    - menuitem \"comps-analysis Prompt skill from comps-analysis.\":\n      - generic: comps-analysis\n      - generic: Prompt skill from comps-analysis.\n    - 'menuitem \"computer_execute_token Execute a previously queued desktop action by token. Use only after the user explicitly confirms the exact token/action in the current conversation. Args: {token:string}.\"':\n      - generic: computer_execute_token\n      - generic: \"Execute a previously queued desktop action by token. Use only after the user explicitly confirms the exact token/action in the current conversation. Args: {token:string}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"computer_observe Observe the real desktop automation status and optionally capture a screenshot or UIA semantic tree. Args: {capture?: bool, uia?: bool}. Returns screen size, cursor, screenshot path/size, and optionally a bounded control tree; omits base64 image data to save context.\"':\n      - generic: computer_observe\n      - generic: \"Observe the real desktop automation status and optionally capture a screenshot or UIA semantic tree. Args: {capture?: bool, uia?: bool}. Returns screen size, cursor, screenshot path/size, and optionally a bounded control tree; omits base64 image data to save context.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"computer_plan_next For an agent conversation: generate queued candidate desktop actions for a natural-language goal. Args: {goal: string, capture?: bool, use_vision?: bool, model_id?: string}. Returns suggestions with confirmation tokens; does not execute them.\"':\n      - generic: computer_plan_next\n      - generic: \"For an agent conversation: generate queued candidate desktop actions for a natural-language goal. Args: {goal: string, capture?: bool, use_vision?: bool, model_id?: string}. Returns suggestions with confirmation tokens; does not execute them.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"computer_preview_action Validate and queue exactly one desktop action without executing. Args: {action:{action:''click''|''move''|''type''|''key''|''wait'', ...}}. Returns risk and a short-lived token for later confirmation.\"':\n      - generic: computer_preview_action\n      - generic: \"Validate and queue exactly one desktop action without executing. Args: {action:{action:'click'|'move'|'type'|'key'|'wait', ...}}. Returns risk and a short-lived token for later confirmation.\"\n    - menuitem \"computer_uia_find Find desktop controls by visible name, control type, class name, or automation id using Windows UI Automation. Read-only; returned centers can be used with previewed mouse actions.\":\n      - generic: computer_uia_find\n      - generic: Find desktop controls by visible name, control type, class name, or automation id using Windows UI Automation. Read-only; returned centers can be used with previewed mouse actions.\n    - menuitem \"computer_uia_status Report whether Windows UI Automation semantic desktop inspection is available. Read-only.\":\n      - generic: computer_uia_status\n      - generic: Report whether Windows UI Automation semantic desktop inspection is available. Read-only.\n    - 'menuitem \"computer_uia_tree Return a bounded Windows UI Automation control tree for the foreground window or desktop root. Read-only. Args: {root?: ''foreground''|''desktop'', max_depth?, max_nodes?, include_offscreen?}.\"':\n      - generic: computer_uia_tree\n      - generic: \"Return a bounded Windows UI Automation control tree for the foreground window or desktop root. Read-only. Args: {root?: 'foreground'|'desktop', max_depth?, max_nodes?, include_offscreen?}.\"\n    - menuitem \"computer_use_loop Autonomous perception-action loop for desktop automation. Screenshots → vision planner → action → verify. Requires vision-capable planner + pyautogui.\":\n      - generic: computer_use_loop\n      - generic: Autonomous perception-action loop for desktop automation. Screenshots → vision planner → action → verify. Requires vision-capable planner + pyautogui.\n    - 'menuitem \"count_words 用途: 对一段已经在手上的文本计算 chars / words / lines 三项；常用于 demo / 兜底统计。 何时不用: 要统计文件用 read_file 取出后再传入；要分词或自然语言分析用 ipython 跑专用库；只是想核对文件大小用 file_stats。 关键参数: text (必填, 直接传字符串)。 示例: count_words({\\\"text\\\": \\\"hello world\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: count_words\n      - generic: \"用途: 对一段已经在手上的文本计算 chars / words / lines 三项；常用于 demo / 兜底统计。 何时不用: 要统计文件用 read_file 取出后再传入；要分词或自然语言分析用 ipython 跑专用库；只是想核对文件大小用 file_stats。 关键参数: text (必填, 直接传字符串)。 示例: count_words({\\\"text\\\": \\\"hello world\\\"})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"crawl_site Purpose: crawl from a seed URL with a bounded queue, URL de-dupe, domain limits, optional robots.txt checks, delay, HTML link discovery, main-content extraction, and JSONL output. Use this for small-to-medium site discovery jobs, not for high-volume distributed scraping. Key args: start_url required; max_pages default 20; max_depth default 2; same_domain default true; allowed_domains optional; include_patterns / exclude_patterns optional regex or literal filters; respect_robots default true; delay_ms default 250; render_mode is http|auto|browser (default http; auto retries likely JS apps with Playwright); browser_wait_ms default 500; output_path optional .jsonl; sandbox_dir optional. Example: crawl_site({\\\"start_url\\\":\\\"https://example.com/docs\\\",\\\"max_pages\\\":30,\\\"max_depth\\\":2})\"':\n      - generic: crawl_site\n      - generic: \"Purpose: crawl from a seed URL with a bounded queue, URL de-dupe, domain limits, optional robots.txt checks, delay, HTML link discovery, main-content extraction, and JSONL output. Use this for small-to-medium site discovery jobs, not for high-volume distributed scraping. Key args: start_url required; max_pages default 20; max_depth default 2; same_domain default true; allowed_domains optional; include_patterns / exclude_patterns optional regex or literal filters; respect_robots default true; delay_ms default 250; render_mode is http|auto|browser (default http; auto retries likely JS apps with Playwright); browser_wait_ms default 500; output_path optional .jsonl; sandbox_dir optional. Example: crawl_site({\\\"start_url\\\":\\\"https://example.com/docs\\\",\\\"max_pages\\\":30,\\\"max_depth\\\":2})\"\n    - menuitem \"creative-3d-animation 把故事创意转成角色、场景、镜头、动作与合成一致的 3D 动画短片制作方案。\":\n      - generic: creative-3d-animation\n      - generic: 把故事创意转成角色、场景、镜头、动作与合成一致的 3D 动画短片制作方案。\n    - menuitem \"creative-anime-pv 为动画、游戏或虚拟 IP 设计短篇 PV，包括卖点提炼、分镜、节奏、音乐方向与生成执行清单。\":\n      - generic: creative-anime-pv\n      - generic: 为动画、游戏或虚拟 IP 设计短篇 PV，包括卖点提炼、分镜、节奏、音乐方向与生成执行清单。\n    - menuitem \"creative-anime-style-forge 将角色与场景锻造成一致的原创动画视觉体系，覆盖线条、比例、上色、材质和镜头规则。\"