e\n      - generic: 将课程定位、学习成果和课程结构设计成信息清楚、可转化且可实现的技能课程详情页。\n    - menuitem \"creative-digital-product-film 把真实产品页面、交互路径和动效参考转成准确呈现界面的电影感数字产品宣传片。\":\n      - generic: creative-digital-product-film\n      - generic: 把真实产品页面、交互路径和动效参考转成准确呈现界面的电影感数字产品宣传片。\n    - menuitem \"creative-director-stage 使用 Octopus 3D 导演台编排角色、场景、机位、姿态、走位和运镜；适用于分镜预演、镜头构图和生成视频前的空间验证。\":\n      - generic: creative-director-stage\n      - generic: 使用 Octopus 3D 导演台编排角色、场景、机位、姿态、走位和运镜；适用于分镜预演、镜头构图和生成视频前的空间验证。\n    - menuitem \"creative-documentary 将主题研究、采访与素材组织为事实可追溯的纪录片结构、旁白和镜头计划。\":\n      - generic: creative-documentary\n      - generic: 将主题研究、采访与素材组织为事实可追溯的纪录片结构、旁白和镜头计划。\n    - menuitem \"creative-dodge-game-video 从角色参考图制作四向躲闪关键帧、游戏反馈和短时反应挑战视频。\":\n      - generic: creative-dodge-game-video\n      - generic: 从角色参考图制作四向躲闪关键帧、游戏反馈和短时反应挑战视频。\n    - menuitem \"creative-dotmatrix-brand-motion 根据品牌标志、名称与标语设计点阵字形系统、横版品牌图和动态字效。\":\n      - generic: creative-dotmatrix-brand-motion\n      - generic: 根据品牌标志、名称与标语设计点阵字形系统、横版品牌图和动态字效。\n    - menuitem \"creative-dreamcore-space 设计梦核、阈限空间与超现实后室场景，控制空间规则、情绪线索、镜头漫游和声音氛围。\":\n      - generic: creative-dreamcore-space\n      - generic: 设计梦核、阈限空间与超现实后室场景，控制空间规则、情绪线索、镜头漫游和声音氛围。\n    - menuitem \"creative-dual-player-intro 根据两位玩家名称、角色参考和游戏世界观设计双人游戏菜单开场、选角确认与短视频生成方案。\":\n      - generic: creative-dual-player-intro\n      - generic: 根据两位玩家名称、角色参考和游戏世界观设计双人游戏菜单开场、选角确认与短视频生成方案。\n    - menuitem \"creative-dynamic-poster 将静态海报转为文字清晰、主体关系稳定且可循环的一镜到底动态海报。\":\n      - generic: creative-dynamic-poster\n      - generic: 将静态海报转为文字清晰、主体关系稳定且可循环的一镜到底动态海报。\n    - menuitem \"creative-ecommerce-images 从真实商品素材规划平台合规的电商主图、卖点图、场景图和细节图组。\":\n      - generic: creative-ecommerce-images\n      - generic: 从真实商品素材规划平台合规的电商主图、卖点图、场景图和细节图组。\n    - menuitem \"creative-editor-export 将时间线工程整理为可迁移的剪辑交付包，包含媒体、字幕、代理、命名与兼容性检查。\":\n      - generic: creative-editor-export\n      - generic: 将时间线工程整理为可迁移的剪辑交付包，包含媒体、字幕、代理、命名与兼容性检查。\n    - menuitem \"creative-education-video 把知识目标转成讲解脚本、图解、示例、练习和理解验证，适合课程与科普视频。\":\n      - generic: creative-education-video\n      - generic: 把知识目标转成讲解脚本、图解、示例、练习和理解验证，适合课程与科普视频。\n    - menuitem \"creative-film-score 为角色、场景和叙事段落设计主题动机、配器、速度、动态与音乐进出点。\":\n      - generic: creative-film-score\n      - generic: 为角色、场景和叙事段落设计主题动机、配器、速度、动态与音乐进出点。\n    - menuitem \"creative-fpv-video 设计连续沉浸的第一视角或 FPV 穿越路线、速度曲线、空间节点与一镜到底提示。\":\n      - generic: creative-fpv-video\n      - generic: 设计连续沉浸的第一视角或 FPV 穿越路线、速度曲线、空间节点与一镜到底提示。\n    - menuitem \"creative-h3-prompt-director 把零散的视频目标、参考素材和限制整理成可控的多模态视频生成指令，适合 H3 类视频模型或兼容模型。\":\n      - generic: creative-h3-prompt-director\n      - generic: 把零散的视频目标、参考素材和限制整理成可控的多模态视频生成指令，适合 H3 类视频模型或兼容模型。\n    - menuitem \"creative-image-inpaint 根据遮罩或区域描述完成局部重绘，保持透视、光线、材质、边缘与未编辑区域稳定。\":\n      - generic: creative-image-inpaint\n      - generic: 根据遮罩或区域描述完成局部重绘，保持透视、光线、材质、边缘与未编辑区域稳定。\n    - menuitem \"creative-image-remix 从参考图提取构图、光线、材质与色彩关系，生成保持目标内容原创的新图方案。\":\n      - generic: creative-image-remix\n      - generic: 从参考图提取构图、光线、材质与色彩关系，生成保持目标内容原创的新图方案。\n    - menuitem \"creative-intentional-lowpoly-film 将人物或场景转成有控制的早期低模、笨拙绑定和生硬运镜短片，同时保持主体可识别与审美一致。\":\n      - generic: creative-intentional-lowpoly-film\n      - generic: 将人物或场景转成有控制的早期低模、笨拙绑定和生硬运镜短片，同时保持主体可识别与审美一致。\n    - menuitem \"creative-koc-video 为 KOC、口播和电商短视频设计开场钩子、自然脚本、镜头、B-roll 与平台版本。\":\n      - generic: creative-koc-video\n      - generic: 为 KOC、口播和电商短视频设计开场钩子、自然脚本、镜头、B-roll 与平台版本。\n    - menuitem \"creative-lighting-studio 为人物、产品与场景设计有动机的光线方向、软硬、比例、色温和空间层次。\":\n      - generic: creative-lighting-studio\n      - generic: 为人物、产品与场景设计有动机的光线方向、软硬、比例、色温和空间层次。\n    - menuitem \"creative-line-explainer 把教材、知识主题或抽象概念转成线条人物、图标和关系图驱动的科普视频。\":\n      - generic: creative-line-explainer\n      - generic: 把教材、知识主题或抽象概念转成线条人物、图标和关系图驱动的科普视频。\n    - menuitem \"creative-lip-makeup-ad 为唇部彩妆与近景美妆产品设计人物、产品、道具互动自然的横屏或竖屏广告。\":\n      - generic: creative-lip-makeup-ad\n      - generic: 为唇部彩妆与近景美妆产品设计人物、产品、道具互动自然的横屏或竖屏广告。\n    - menuitem \"creative-liveaction-drawing-reveal 让真实照片或视频先自然运动，再由绘制动作把主体显影为手绘层并保持空间一致。\":\n      - generic: creative-liveaction-drawing-reveal\n      - generic: 让真实照片或视频先自然运动，再由绘制动作把主体显影为手绘层并保持空间一致。\n    - menuitem \"creative-localization-dubbing 将短剧或视频本地化为目标语言，保持角色音色、语气、时长、口型与字幕同步。\":\n      - generic: creative-localization-dubbing\n      - generic: 将短剧或视频本地化为目标语言，保持角色音色、语气、时长、口型与字幕同步。\n    - menuitem \"creative-microdrama-writer 从选题和人物关系开发可连续生产的微短剧剧集，覆盖钩子、冲突、反转、集尾与制作约束。\":\n      - generic: creative-microdrama-writer\n      - generic: 从选题和人物关系开发可连续生产的微短剧剧集，覆盖钩子、冲突、反转、集尾与制作约束。\n    - menuitem \"creative-multi-angle-render 从单张或少量参考建立主体结构假设并生成前后左右、俯仰与三分之四视角。\":\n      - generic: creative-multi-angle-render\n      - generic: 从单张或少量参考建立主体结构假设并生成前后左右、俯仰与三分之四视角。\n    - menuitem \"creative-multiboard 将故事拆成多宫格分镜整图，保持镜头顺序、角色一致、空间方向和阅读节奏。\":\n      - generic: creative-multiboard\n      - generic: 将故事拆成多宫格分镜整图，保持镜头顺序、角色一致、空间方向和阅读节奏。\n    - menuitem \"creative-music-video 从歌曲结构设计 MV 的表演、空间、造型、剪辑、动态字幕与生成路线。\":\n      - generic: creative-music-video\n      - generic: 从歌曲结构设计 MV 的表演、空间、造型、剪辑、动态字幕与生成路线。\n    - menuitem \"creative-paper-collage 将文案或知识主题转成纸张拼贴、分层布景与触感声音统一的讲解动画。\":\n      - generic: creative-paper-collage\n      - generic: 将文案或知识主题转成纸张拼贴、分层布景与触感声音统一的讲解动画。\n    - menuitem \"creative-paper-stopmotion-explainer 把知识主题转成纸偶、分层布景、逐帧动作和实物音效统一的定格科普视频制作包。\":\n      - generic: creative-paper-stopmotion-explainer\n      - generic: 把知识主题转成纸偶、分层布景、逐帧动作和实物音效统一的定格科普视频制作包。\n    - menuitem \"creative-pixel-block-art 将图像或概念转换为可搭建的体素/方块画，控制网格、调色板、轮廓与材料数量。\":\n      - generic: creative-pixel-block-art\n      - generic: 将图像或概念转换为可搭建的体素/方块画，控制网格、调色板、轮廓与材料数量。\n    - menuitem \"creative-podcast-kit 将播客录音或转录稿整理为节目说明、章节、短视频切片、文章与社媒内容包。\":\n      - generic: creative-podcast-kit\n      - generic: 将播客录音或转录稿整理为节目说明、章节、短视频切片、文章与社媒内容包。\n    - menuitem \"creative-product-ad 从产品图片与卖点制作极简、可信、可转化的产品广告镜头与多渠道变体。\":\n      - generic: creative-product-ad\n      - generic: 从产品图片与卖点制作极简、可信、可转化的产品广告镜头与多渠道变体。\n    - menuitem \"creative-promo-video 把产品或服务简介转成可执行的宣传视频方案，覆盖受众、卖点、证据、镜头与多渠道版本。\":\n      - generic: creative-promo-video\n      - generic: 把产品或服务简介转成可执行的宣传视频方案，覆盖受众、卖点、证据、镜头与多渠道版本。\n    - menuitem \"creative-silkscreen-film 将主题转成丝印装饰插画、有限色版、颗粒套印与同步音效统一的短片。\":\n      - generic: creative-silkscreen-film\n      - generic: 将主题转成丝印装饰插画、有限色版、颗粒套印与同步音效统一的短片。\n    - menuitem \"creative-sleep-audio 设计助眠冥想、环境声与轻声引导音频，控制节奏、动态、循环与刺激性。\":\n      - generic: creative-sleep-audio\n      - generic: 设计助眠冥想、环境声与轻声引导音频，控制节奏、动态、循环与刺激性。\n    - menuitem \"creative-storyboard-assets 把剧本与参考图整理为角色、场景、道具和镜头统一的综合设定板。\":\n      - generic: creative-storyboard-assets\n      - generic: 把剧本与参考图整理为角色、场景、道具和镜头统一的综合设定板。\n    - menuitem \"creative-title-sequence 设计电影、短剧或节目片头，包括叙事母题、字体系统、演职员表、转场和视效节奏。\":\n      - generic: creative-title-sequence\n      - generic: 设计电影、短剧或节目片头，包括叙事母题、字体系统、演职员表、转场和视效节奏。\n    - menuitem \"creative-toy-grid-poster 将角色参考制作成身份一致的 3D 潮玩六宫格动态海报，适合 IP 提案和社媒展示。\":\n      - generic: creative-toy-grid-poster\n      - generic: 将角色参考制作成身份一致的 3D 潮玩六宫格动态海报，适合 IP 提案和社媒展示。\n    - menuitem \"creative-ui-motion 将产品界面和功能流程转成品牌一致的 UI 动效广告、功能演示与动态分镜。\":\n      - generic: creative-ui-motion\n      - generic: 将产品界面和功能流程转成品牌一致的 UI 动效广告、功能演示与动态分镜。\n    - menuitem \"creative-video-deconstruct 逆向拆解参考视频的镜头、节奏、视觉技术、声音、制作难度与可复用创作规则。\":\n      - generic: creative-video-deconstruct\n      - generic: 逆向拆解参考视频的镜头、节奏、视觉技术、声音、制作难度与可复用创作规则。\n    - menuitem \"creative-video-editor 在 Octopus AI 剪辑工坊中读取和修改多轨视频项目，并对节奏、转场、字幕、调色、效果、关键帧、变速和成片导出做基于真实画面的编辑判断；适用于剪辑、时间线诊断、视觉复核与可撤销批量编辑。\":\n      - generic: creative-video-editor\n      - generic: 在 Octopus AI 剪辑工坊中读取和修改多轨视频项目，并对节奏、转场、字幕、调色、效果、关键帧、变速和成片导出做基于真实画面的编辑判断；适用于剪辑、时间线诊断、视觉复核与可撤销批量编辑。\n    - menuitem \"creative-visual-direction 为图像、视频和动态设计建立统一的构图、色彩、材质、字体、光线与运动语言。\":\n      - generic: creative-visual-direction\n      - generic: 为图像、视频和动态设计建立统一的构图、色彩、材质、字体、光线与运动语言。\n    - menuitem \"creative-voice-design 用角色背景、表演意图和声学参数设计可试听的原创音色方向。\":\n      - generic: creative-voice-design\n      - generic: 用角色背景、表演意图和声学参数设计可试听的原创音色方向。\n    - menuitem \"creative-vox-explainer 把主题、文章或报告转成带旁白、字幕、图解和拼贴节奏的高密度科普短片。\":\n      - generic: creative-vox-explainer\n      - generic: 把主题、文章或报告转成带旁白、字幕、图解和拼贴节奏的高密度科普短片。\n    - menuitem \"creative-zodiac-english-series 围绕十二生肖或其他文化角色体系设计儿童英语故事、儿歌、重复句型和连续剧集资产。\":\n      - generic: creative-zodiac-english-series\n      - generic: 围绕十二生肖或其他文化角色体系设计儿童英语故事、儿歌、重复句型和连续剧集资产。\n    - menuitem \"crop_and_replicate_assets_in_image Crop detected or provided image asset boxes into PNG files.\":\n      - generic: crop_and_replicate_assets_in_image\n      - generic: Crop detected or provided image asset boxes into PNG files.\n    - menuitem \"cross-platform-adapter Adapts and repurposes content (blog posts, articles, reports, newsletters) for LinkedIn, Twitter/X, WeChat Official Accounts, Zhihu, and Slack — adjusting tone, length, formatting, and language to match each platform's norms, including English-Chinese cross-language adaptation. Use when a user wants to repurpose, cross-post, adapt, or convert existing content for different platforms.\":\n      - generic: cross-platform-adapter\n      - generic: Adapts and repurposes content (blog posts, articles, reports, newsletters) for LinkedIn, Twitter/X, WeChat Official Accounts, Zhihu, and Slack — adjusting tone, length, formatting, and language to match each platform's norms, including English-Chinese cross-language adaptation. Use when a user wants to repurpose, cross-post, adapt, or convert existing content for different platforms.\n    - menuitem \"data-viz-renderer Generate self-contained HTML/SVG infographics from JSON data, including stat cards, bar charts, flow diagrams, and mixed dashboards. Offers 8 color palettes and built-in icons with no external dependencies. Triggered when users request data visualization, infographics, charts, or dashboards.\":\n      - generic: data-viz-renderer\n      - generic: Generate self-contained HTML/SVG infographics from JSON data, including stat cards, bar charts, flow diagrams, and mixed dashboards. Offers 8 color palettes and built-in icons with no external dependencies. Triggered when users request data visualization, infographics, charts, or dashboards.\n    - 'menuitem \"database-scout Explore SQLite and PostgreSQL databases: list tables, inspect schemas (columns/types/constraints), preview data, generate Mermaid ER diagrams, and run safe read-only queries. Triggered by requests to explore a database, view table structures, describe tables, generate diagrams, or query data, and by keywords like database exploration, schema, ER diagram, or SQL query.\"':\n      - generic: database-scout\n      - generic: \"Explore SQLite and PostgreSQL databases: list tables, inspect schemas (columns/types/constraints), preview data, generate Mermaid ER diagrams, and run safe read-only queries. Triggered by requests to explore a database, view table structures, describe tables, generate diagrams, or query data, and by keywords like database exploration, schema, ER diagram, or SQL query.\"\n    - menuitem \"deck-refresh Updates a presentation with new numbers — quarterly refreshes, earnings updates, comp rolls, rebased market data. Use whenever the user asks to \\\"update the deck with Q4 numbers\\\", \\\"refresh the comps\\\", \\\"roll this forward\\\", \\\"swap in the new earnings\\\", \\\"change all the $485M to $512M\\\", or any request to swap figures across an existing deck without rebuilding it.\":\n      - generic: deck-refresh\n      - generic: Updates a presentation with new numbers — quarterly refreshes, earnings updates, comp rolls, rebased market data. Use whenever the user asks to \"update the deck with Q4 numbers\", \"refresh the comps\", \"roll this forward\", \"swap in the new earnings\", \"change all the $485M to $512M\", or any request to swap figures across an existing deck without rebuilding it.\n    - 'menuitem \"deep_evolve B3 deep self-evolution · MiniMax-style autonomous loop. Each round: LLM proposes K candidate SOUL changes → judges each candidate''s predicted impact → picks winner → optionally applies. EXPENSIVE (~10-30¢ per run · uses haiku-tier model). Default `dry_run=True` returns the full plan without mutating SOUL — review the proposed changes first, then re-run with `dry_run=False` to actually apply. Args: {window?: int (default 20), candidates_per_round?: int (1-5, default 3), max_rounds?: int (1-10, default 1), dry_run?: bool (default True)}. Returns full audit trail: all proposals, judgments, applied actions, and total cost.\"':\n      - generic: deep_evolve\n      - generic: \"B3 deep self-evolution · MiniMax-style autonomous loop. Each round: LLM proposes K candidate SOUL changes → judges each candidate's predicted impact → picks winner → optionally applies. EXPENSIVE (~10-30¢ per run · uses haiku-tier model). Default `dry_run=True` returns the full plan without mutating SOUL — review the proposed changes first, then re-run with `dry_run=False` to actually apply. Args: {window?: int (default 20), candidates_per_round?: int (1-5, default 3), max_rounds?: int (1-10, default 1), dry_run?: bool (default True)}. Returns full audit trail: all proposals, judgments, applied actions, and total cost.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"deep_reflect B2 self-evaluation · LLM-judged review of recent scored turns. Reads the last `window` turns + current SOUL, sends a single judging call to a cheap model (~2-3¢), returns structured envelope: {verdict: {overall_score 0-100, trend, dominant_failure_mode, lesson_quality, action: add_lesson|revert_last|no_action, action_detail, rationale}}. Use this when the heuristic `analyze_soul_impact` says ''inconclusive'' but you want a real LLM opinion before acting. Args: {window?: int (default 20), model?: string}.\"':\n      - generic: deep_reflect\n      - generic: \"B2 self-evaluation · LLM-judged review of recent scored turns. Reads the last `window` turns + current SOUL, sends a single judging call to a cheap model (~2-3¢), returns structured envelope: {verdict: {overall_score 0-100, trend, dominant_failure_mode, lesson_quality, action: add_lesson|revert_last|no_action, action_detail, rationale}}. Use this when the heuristic `analyze_soul_impact` says 'inconclusive' but you want a real LLM opinion before acting. Args: {window?: int (default 20), model?: string}.\"\n    - menuitem \"deep-module-refactor Explore a codebase to find opportunities for architectural improvement, focusing on making the codebase more testable by deepening shallow modules. Use when user wants to improve architecture, find refactoring opportunities, consolidate tightly-coupled modules, or make a codebase more AI-navigable.\":\n      - generic: deep-module-refactor\n      - generic: Explore a codebase to find opportunities for architectural improvement, focusing on making the codebase more testable by deepening shallow modules. Use when user wants to improve architecture, find refactoring opportunities, consolidate tightly-coupled modules, or make a codebase more AI-navigable.\n    - menuitem \"deep-probe 对用户的方案或设计进行连环追问，逐一排查决策树的每个分支，直到双方达成共识。当用户希望压力测试某个方案、被深度质询设计思路，或提到“帮我审一下”、“追问一下”、“挑挑毛病”等关键词时触发。\":\n      - generic: deep-probe\n      - generic: 对用户的方案或设计进行连环追问，逐一排查决策树的每个分支，直到双方达成共识。当用户希望压力测试某个方案、被深度质询设计思路，或提到“帮我审一下”、“追问一下”、“挑挑毛病”等关键词时触发。\n    - menuitem:\n      - generic: deep-research-swarm\n      - generic: \"Multi-agent deep research orchestration with adaptive routing. Use this skill whenever comprehensive, multi-dimensional, evidence-backed investigation is required — competitive intelligence, market analysis, controversy investigation, policy evaluation, academic landscape review, risk assessment, file-based analysis, or any task demanding cross-verified, multi-source findings. **Route Classification** (Phase 0 auto-determines): - **Route A — Wide Search**: Broad/exploratory topics where search breadth is critical (e.g., industry landscape, trend survey, competitive mapping, \\\"help me research industry XX\\\"). First deploy multi-agent wide exploration to maximize coverage, then multi-agent deep dive per dimension. Two-stage parallel swarm. - **Route B — Focused Search**: Specific questions with clear dimensions or a narrow topic. Standard pipeline: landscape scan → decompose → parallel deep dive. - **Route C — File-Only Research**: User uploads files and explicitly requests analysis based solely on file content (signals: \\\"based on these files only\\\", \\\"analyze only the uploaded documents\\\", \\\"no external search\\\", \\\"just based on these files\\\"). NO external search — multi-file deep analysis, cross-file insight extraction, then handoff to writing skill. - **Route D — File-Augmented Research**: User uploads files as reference or starting point, but does not restrict to file content only (signals: \\\"refer to these files\\\", \\\"combine with files\\\", \\\"help me complete this\\\", \\\"based on this, write...\\\", or simply no explicit restriction). Primarily analyze files, supplement with professional external sources for additional context and verification, then synthesize and write. Trigger Rule: When the user uses terms such as: - research, investigation, in-depth analysis, comprehensive analysis - trend analysis, comparative analysis, comparison, evaluation, assessment - future prediction, forecasting, industry outlook, market outlook Or when the user uploads files requesting research/analysis/report generation. You MUST load the `deep-research` capability skill before proceeding. Do NOT use for: simple factual lookup, single-source Q&A.\"\n    - menuitem \"deploy_website Publish a local static website directory to Octopus' local deployments area.\":\n      - generic: deploy_website\n      - generic: Publish a local static website directory to Octopus' local deployments area.\n    - 'menuitem \"diary_write Append a timestamped entry to today''s diary file (`diary/YYYY-MM-DD.md`) for the current agent.\"':\n      - generic: diary_write\n      - generic: \"Append a timestamped entry to today's diary file (`diary/YYYY-MM-DD.md`) for the current agent.\"\n    - menuitem \"director_stage.scene_get 读取 3D 导演台场景。参数 scene_id 必填；view 可选 summary/entities/timeline/full。返回角色、相机、姿态和时间线路径。\":\n      - generic: director_stage.scene_get\n      - generic: 读取 3D 导演台场景。参数 scene_id 必填；view 可选 summary/entities/timeline/full。返回角色、相机、姿态和时间线路径。\n    - 'menuitem \"edit_file 用途: 安全的精确编辑 — 把 old_string 替换为 new_string，默认要求文件中只出现一次 (避免误改)。改源码首选。 何时不用: 要一次性应用多处不同替换用 multi_edit_file (原子化、按序合并)；要写全新文件用 write_text_file；只是末尾追加用 append_text_file；宽松全替换用 edit_text_file。 关键参数: path / old_string / new_string (均必填, old≠new); replace_all (默认 False, True 时允许多处匹配并全替换)。 示例: edit_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"a.py\\\", \\\"old_string\\\": \\\"def foo():\\\\n pass\\\", \\\"new_string\\\": \\\"def foo():\\\\n return 1\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: edit_file\n      - generic: \"用途: 安全的精确编辑 — 把 old_string 替换为 new_string，默认要求文件中只出现一次 (避免误改)。改源码首选。 何时不用: 要一次性应用多处不同替换用 multi_edit_file (原子化、按序合并)；要写全新文件用 write_text_file；只是末尾追加用 append_text_file；宽松全替换用 edit_text_file。 关键参数: path / old_string / new_string (均必填, old≠new); replace_all (默认 False, True 时允许多处匹配并全替换)。 示例: edit_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"a.py\\\", \\\"old_string\\\": \\\"def foo():\\\\n pass\\\", \\\"new_string\\\": \\\"def foo():\\\\n return 1\\\"})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"edit_text_file 用途: 老式宽松版 find-and-replace — 不强制唯一性，按计数替换出现的字面串。适合简单批量改名、注释清理。 何时不用: 想要「唯一片段才替换」的安全编辑用 edit_file；要一次改多处不同片段用 multi_edit_file；要写新文件用 write_text_file。 关键参数: path / find / replace (均必填); count (默认 -1 = 全部替换, 正数 = 只替换前 N 个)。 示例: edit_text_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"a.py\\\", \\\"find\\\": \\\"foo\\\", \\\"replace\\\": \\\"bar\\\", \\\"count\\\": 1})\"':\n      - generic: edit_text_file\n      - generic: \"用途: 老式宽松版 find-and-replace — 不强制唯一性，按计数替换出现的字面串。适合简单批量改名、注释清理。 何时不用: 想要「唯一片段才替换」的安全编辑用 edit_file；要一次改多处不同片段用 multi_edit_file；要写新文件用 write_text_file。 关键参数: path / find / replace (均必填); count (默认 -1 = 全部替换, 正数 = 只替换前 N 个)。 示例: edit_text_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"a.py\\\", \\\"find\\\": \\\"foo\\\", \\\"replace\\\": \\\"bar\\\", \\\"count\\\": 1})\"\n    - menuitem \"email-manager 收发和管理邮件，支持查看未读邮件、搜索邮件、下载附件、发送带附件的邮件，并提供交互式配置向导。兼容Gmail、Outlook、163.com、126.com、QQ邮箱等主流服务商。当用户需要收发邮件、查看收件箱、搜索特定邮件、管理附件，或提及配置邮箱时触发。\":\n      - generic: email-manager\n      - generic: 收发和管理邮件，支持查看未读邮件、搜索邮件、下载附件、发送带附件的邮件，并提供交互式配置向导。兼容Gmail、Outlook、163.com、126.com、QQ邮箱等主流服务商。当用户需要收发邮件、查看收件箱、搜索特定邮件、管理附件，或提及配置邮箱时触发。\n    - 'menuitem \"email-to-calendar Extract calendar events and deadlines from emails and create calendar entries. Two modes: monitor your inbox directly, or process emails you forward to a dedicated address. Trigger when a user asks to scan emails for events, mentions an event in an email, or wants to add something from an email to their calendar.\"':\n      - generic: email-to-calendar\n      - generic: \"Extract calendar events and deadlines from emails and create calendar entries. Two modes: monitor your inbox directly, or process emails you forward to a dedicated address. Trigger when a user asks to scan emails for events, mentions an event in an email, or wants to add something from an email to their calendar.\"\n    - menuitem \"equity-research Generate comprehensive equity research snapshots combining analyst consensus estimates, company fundamentals, historical prices, and macroeconomic context. Use when researching stocks, comparing estimates to actuals, analyzing company financials, assessing equity valuations, or building investment cases.\":\n      - generic: equity-research\n      - generic: Generate comprehensive equity research snapshots combining analyst consensus estimates, company fundamentals, historical prices, and macroeconomic context. Use when researching stocks, comparing estimates to actuals, analyzing company financials, assessing equity valuations, or building investment cases.\n    - 'menuitem \"exec_shell 用途: 执行本地 shell 命令 (无 shell=True、有超时)；最适合编译、打包、文件管线、调用各种 CLI；当没有专门 skill 匹配时的兜底。 何时不用: 谷歌/搜资料用 web_search；抓取已知 URL 用 fetch_url (curl/wget 抓回的 HTML 不好解析)；跑 Python 片段用 ipython；改文件用 edit_file/write_text_file；查 git 状态用 git_status。 关键参数: command (str 或 list[str], 必填); cwd (可选); timeout_s (默认 60); run_in_background (默认 False, True 时返回 task_id, 配合 read_shell_output / kill_shell)。不要写 `cd dir && command` 或 `2>&1`：本工具不会启动 shell；请把 dir 放入 cwd，stdout/stderr 会分别返回。 网络: 沙箱内默认禁止网络访问（pnpm/npm/pip 等需联网的命令会失败，仅模型推理端点可达）。网络有三档：默认禁网；传 allow_network=true 完全开启；若只需安装依赖/拉取代码等开发工具场景，可传 egress_allow_common=true（放行 npm/pip/github/apt 等预置常用域名，其余仍拦截）。 示例: exec_shell({\\\"command\\\": \\\"npm test\\\", \\\"cwd\\\": \\\"web\\\", \\\"timeout_s\\\": 120})\"':\n      - generic: exec_shell\n      - generic: \"用途: 执行本地 shell 命令 (无 shell=True、有超时)；最适合编译、打包、文件管线、调用各种 CLI；当没有专门 skill 匹配时的兜底。 何时不用: 谷歌/搜资料用 web_search；抓取已知 URL 用 fetch_url (curl/wget 抓回的 HTML 不好解析)；跑 Python 片段用 ipython；改文件用 edit_file/write_text_file；查 git 状态用 git_status。 关键参数: command (str 或 list[str], 必填); cwd (可选); timeout_s (默认 60); run_in_background (默认 False, True 时返回 task_id, 配合 read_shell_output / kill_shell)。不要写 `cd dir && command` 或 `2>&1`：本工具不会启动 shell；请把 dir 放入 cwd，stdout/stderr 会分别返回。 网络: 沙箱内默认禁止网络访问（pnpm/npm/pip 等需联网的命令会失败，仅模型推理端点可达）。网络有三档：默认禁网；传 allow_network=true 完全开启；若只需安装依赖/拉取代码等开发工具场景，可传 egress_allow_common=true（放行 npm/pip/github/apt 等预置常用域名，其余仍拦截）。 示例: exec_shell({\\\"command\\\": \\\"npm test\\\", \\\"cwd\\\": \\\"web\\\", \\\"timeout_s\\\": 120})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"execute_skill Purpose: execute an enabled read-only skill discovered via search_skills when that skill was omitted from the compact/native tool catalog. Side-effecting, dangerous, meta, disabled, or ambiguously tagged skills are rejected and must use the normal tool/capability path. Key params: name (required), args (object, default {}). Example: execute_skill({\\\"name\\\": \\\"code_search\\\", \\\"args\\\": {\\\"query\\\": \\\"TODO\\\"}})\"':\n      - generic: execute_skill\n      - generic: \"Purpose: execute an enabled read-only skill discovered via search_skills when that skill was omitted from the compact/native tool catalog. Side-effecting, dangerous, meta, disabled, or ambiguously tagged skills are rejected and must use the normal tool/capability path. Key params: name (required), args (object, default {}). Example: execute_skill({\\\"name\\\": \\\"code_search\\\", \\\"args\\\": {\\\"query\\\": \\\"TODO\\\"}})\"\n    - menuitem \"exit_plan_mode Transition the current thread from plan mode to a write-capable tier (chat/team/code) after a plan has been confirmed.\":\n      - generic: exit_plan_mode\n      - generic: Transition the current thread from plan mode to a write-capable tier (chat/team/code) after a plan has been confirmed.\n    - menuitem \"fast-browser-use Fastest browser automation with anti-bot bypass and DOM extraction. Navigate pages, capture screenshots, manage sessions, and harvest data from infinite scroll via Chrome DevTools Protocol. Runs 10x faster than Puppeteer. Trigger for any web scraping, automated browsing, data extraction, or screenshot task.\":\n      - generic: fast-browser-use\n      - generic: Fastest browser automation with anti-bot bypass and DOM extraction. Navigate pages, capture screenshots, manage sessions, and harvest data from infinite scroll via Chrome DevTools Protocol. Runs 10x faster than Puppeteer. Trigger for any web scraping, automated browsing, data extraction, or screenshot task.\n    - 'menuitem \"fetch_url 用途: 对一个已知 URL 发 HTTP GET；默认返回原始 body 文本 (有上限)。开 extract=true 走 trafilatura 抽取正文 + 元数据 (title/author/date/sitename/description/language)，把导航/广告/页脚剥掉。 何时不用: 不知道目标网址、要先「搜一下」用 web_search；要执行本地命令用 exec_shell (curl/wget 不要绕道这里)；私网地址默认被 SSRF 拦截，需要时显式 allow_private=true。 关键参数: url (必填); extract (默认 False, 阅读文章问答时建议 True); timeout_ms (默认 5000); max_bytes (默认 100000)。 示例: fetch_url({\\\"url\\\": \\\"https://example.com/post\\\", \\\"extract\\\": true})\"':\n      - generic: fetch_url\n      - generic: \"用途: 对一个已知 URL 发 HTTP GET；默认返回原始 body 文本 (有上限)。开 extract=true 走 trafilatura 抽取正文 + 元数据 (title/author/date/sitename/description/language)，把导航/广告/页脚剥掉。 何时不用: 不知道目标网址、要先「搜一下」用 web_search；要执行本地命令用 exec_shell (curl/wget 不要绕道这里)；私网地址默认被 SSRF 拦截，需要时显式 allow_private=true。 关键参数: url (必填); extract (默认 False, 阅读文章问答时建议 True); timeout_ms (默认 5000); max_bytes (默认 100000)。 示例: fetch_url({\\\"url\\\": \\\"https://example.com/post\\\", \\\"extract\\\": true})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"file_stats 用途: 不读内容，只取一个文件/目录的元数据 (size, mtime, is_file, is_dir)；判断存在性、大小、最近修改时间。 何时不用: 要看内容用 read_file；要看目录里有什么用 list_cwd 或 tree；要批量按 pattern 找用 glob_files。 关键参数: path (必填); cwd (相对路径基准, 可选)。 示例: file_stats({\\\"path\\\": \\\"README.md\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: file_stats\n      - generic: \"用途: 不读内容，只取一个文件/目录的元数据 (size, mtime, is_file, is_dir)；判断存在性、大小、最近修改时间。 何时不用: 要看内容用 read_file；要看目录里有什么用 list_cwd 或 tree；要批量按 pattern 找用 glob_files。 关键参数: path (必填); cwd (相对路径基准, 可选)。 示例: file_stats({\\\"path\\\": \\\"README.md\\\"})\"\n    - menuitem \"find_asset_bbox Detect non-background asset bounding boxes in an image.\":\n      - generic: find_asset_bbox\n      - generic: Detect non-background asset bounding boxes in an image.\n    - menuitem \"format_code Run formatter (auto-detects ruff format/prettier). Default check-only.\":\n      - generic: format_code\n      - generic: Run formatter (auto-detects ruff format/prettier). Default check-only.\n    - menuitem \"frontend-design 前端设计技能，包含 UI/UX 设计原则、响应式设计、设计系统构建。在设计界面或实现设计时调用。\":\n      - generic: frontend-design\n      - generic: 前端设计技能，包含 UI/UX 设计原则、响应式设计、设计系统构建。在设计界面或实现设计时调用。\n    - menuitem \"frontend-ui-engineering Builds production-quality UIs. Use when building or modifying user-facing interfaces. Use when creating components, implementing layouts, managing state, or when the output needs to look and feel production-quality rather than AI-generated.\":\n      - generic: frontend-ui-engineering\n      - generic: Builds production-quality UIs. Use when building or modifying user-facing interfaces. Use when creating components, implementing layouts, managing state, or when the output needs to look and feel production-quality rather than AI-generated.\n    - menuitem \"gantt-chart-builder 根据任务列表和依赖关系生成交互式HTML甘特图，支持关键路径分析（CPM），可视化项目时间线、依赖关系和可延迟的浮动时间。当用户提到甘特图、项目时间线、关键路径、任务排期、项目进度图、依赖关系可视化、工期计算或直接说“帮我排一下项目时间”、“生成一个项目进度图”、“分析一下哪些任务是关键路径”时触发。\":\n      - generic: gantt-chart-builder\n      - generic: 根据任务列表和依赖关系生成交互式HTML甘特图，支持关键路径分析（CPM），可视化项目时间线、依赖关系和可延迟的浮动时间。当用户提到甘特图、项目时间线、关键路径、任务排期、项目进度图、依赖关系可视化、工期计算或直接说“帮我排一下项目时间”、“生成一个项目进度图”、“分析一下哪些任务是关键路径”时触发。\n    - 'menuitem \"general-writing General writing skill — covers fiction, fanfiction, poetry, lyrics, drama, screenplay, essay, game writing, murder mystery, TRPG scenarios, letters, and all other writing genres. Routes to genre-specific sub-skills for execution. Do NOT use for: industry reports, market analysis, policy briefs, consulting deliverables, white papers, technical reports (use report-writing); academic papers, surveys, empirical research, literature reviews (use paper-writing).\"':\n      - generic: general-writing\n      - generic: \"General writing skill — covers fiction, fanfiction, poetry, lyrics, drama, screenplay, essay, game writing, murder mystery, TRPG scenarios, letters, and all other writing genres. Routes to genre-specific sub-skills for execution. Do NOT use for: industry reports, market analysis, policy briefs, consulting deliverables, white papers, technical reports (use report-writing); academic papers, surveys, empirical research, literature reviews (use paper-writing).\"\n    - menuitem \"generate_image Directly generate an image with the trusted Agnes/Volcano media provider; use this executable tool for image creation instead of activating an image skill pack.\":\n      - generic: generate_image\n      - generic: Directly generate an image with the trusted Agnes/Volcano media provider; use this executable tool for image creation instead of activating an image skill pack.\n    - menuitem \"generate_sound_effects Generate sound effects via a configured audio provider.\":\n      - generic: generate_sound_effects\n      - generic: Generate sound effects via a configured audio provider.\n    - menuitem \"generate_speech Generate speech via a configured TTS provider.\":\n      - generic: generate_speech\n      - generic: Generate speech via a configured TTS provider.\n    - menuitem \"generate_video Directly generate a video with the trusted Agnes/Volcano media provider; use this executable tool for video creation instead of activating a video skill pack.\":\n      - generic: generate_video\n      - generic: Directly generate a video with the trusted Agnes/Volcano media provider; use this executable tool for video creation instead of activating a video skill pack.\n    - menuitem \"get_available_voices List voice ids supported by the configured TTS provider.\":\n      - generic: get_available_voices\n      - generic: List voice ids supported by the configured TTS provider.\n    - 'menuitem \"get_data_source Fetch data from public adapters: yahoo_finance, arxiv, openalex, crossref.\"':\n      - generic: get_data_source\n      - generic: \"Fetch data from public adapters: yahoo_finance, arxiv, openalex, crossref.\"\n    - menuitem \"get_data_source_desc Describe available public data-source adapters.\":\n      - generic: get_data_source_desc\n      - generic: Describe available public data-source adapters.\n    - menuitem \"git_add Stage explicit paths · rejects -A / '.' / flag injection.\":\n      - generic: git_add\n      - generic: Stage explicit paths · rejects -A / '.' / flag injection.\n    - menuitem \"git_branch List branches · or create a new one (no switch, no force).\":\n      - generic: git_branch\n      - generic: List branches · or create a new one (no switch, no force).\n    - menuitem \"git_commit Commit staged changes (no auto-add, no amend, no hook skip).\":\n      - generic: git_commit\n      - generic: Commit staged changes (no auto-add, no amend, no hook skip).\n    - 'menuitem \"git_diff Run `git diff` (optionally --staged or for a single path).\"':\n      - generic: git_diff\n      - generic: \"Run `git diff` (optionally --staged or for a single path).\"\n    - menuitem \"git_log Recent commits (sha/author/date/subject · structured).\":\n      - generic: git_log\n      - generic: Recent commits (sha/author/date/subject · structured).\n    - 'menuitem \"git_status Structured `git status` (branch + porcelain file list).\"':\n      - generic: git_status\n      - generic: \"Structured `git status` (branch + porcelain file list).\"\n    - menuitem \"github.pr_summary 查看并摘要某个 GitHub PR 的元信息:标题 / 状态 / 增删行数 / 评论数 / 评审状态 / 改动文件数 / 作者 / 链接 / 创建与更新时间。参数:pr_number 必填(整数或 '#123' 形式),repo 可选('owner/name',缺省用当前仓库)。适用于'看下这个 PR'、'PR 123 改了啥'、'这个 PR 评审过了吗'。\":\n      - generic: github.pr_summary\n      - generic: 查看并摘要某个 GitHub PR 的元信息:标题 / 状态 / 增删行数 / 评论数 / 评审状态 / 改动文件数 / 作者 / 链接 / 创建与更新时间。参数:pr_number 必填(整数或 '#123' 形式),repo 可选('owner/name',缺省用当前仓库)。适用于'看下这个 PR'、'PR 123 改了啥'、'这个 PR 评审过了吗'。\n    - menuitem \"gitlab-cli-skills GitLab personal access token with 'api' scope. Used by automation scripts (e.g. post-inline-comment.py) to post MR comments via the REST API. If not set, scripts fall back to reading the token from glab CLI config (~/.config/glab-cli/config.yml).\":\n      - generic: gitlab-cli-skills\n      - generic: GitLab personal access token with 'api' scope. Used by automation scripts (e.g. post-inline-comment.py) to post MR comments via the REST API. If not set, scripts fall back to reading the token from glab CLI config (~/.config/glab-cli/config.yml).\n    - 'menuitem \"glob_files 用途: 按 glob (支持 ** 递归) 列文件，按 mtime 倒序返回；用于「找所有 *.py」「找最新改的 .md」之类。 何时不用: 要按内容 / 正则找用 grep_text；只看一个目录的直接子项用 list_cwd；要看完整树形结构用 tree；知道精确路径直接 read_file。 关键参数: pattern (必填, 例如 ''**/*.py''); root (默认 ''.''); max_results (默认 500, 上限 500); include_dirs (默认 False, 默认只返回文件)。 示例: glob_files({\\\"pattern\\\": \\\"runtime/**/*.py\\\", \\\"root\\\": \\\".\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: glob_files\n      - generic: \"用途: 按 glob (支持 ** 递归) 列文件，按 mtime 倒序返回；用于「找所有 *.py」「找最新改的 .md」之类。 何时不用: 要按内容 / 正则找用 grep_text；只看一个目录的直接子项用 list_cwd；要看完整树形结构用 tree；知道精确路径直接 read_file。 关键参数: pattern (必填, 例如 '**/*.py'); root (默认 '.'); max_results (默认 500, 上限 500); include_dirs (默认 False, 默认只返回文件)。 示例: glob_files({\\\"pattern\\\": \\\"runtime/**/*.py\\\", \\\"root\\\": \\\".\\\"})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"grep_text 用途: 在文本文件里跑 Python 正则搜内容 (不限于代码 — 配置 / 文档 / 日志都行)；返回 [{path, line, text}] 行级匹配。 何时不用: 只想按文件名 / 路径找用 glob_files；要读完整文件用 read_file；要做语义级代码检索用 code_search / lsp_skills；二进制或 >1MB 的文件会被自动跳过。 关键参数: pattern (必填, Python re); root (默认 ''.''); path (可选, 精确文件/目录且优先于注入的 root); glob (默认 ''**/*''); ignore_case (默认 False); max_matches (默认 100, 上限 500); max_files (默认 5000, 上限 20000)。默认跳过 node_modules、dist、build、coverage、虚拟环境和隐藏目录。 示例: grep_text({\\\"pattern\\\": \\\"def register_\\\", \\\"root\\\": \\\"runtime\\\", \\\"glob\\\": \\\"**/*.py\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: grep_text\n      - generic: \"用途: 在文本文件里跑 Python 正则搜内容 (不限于代码 — 配置 / 文档 / 日志都行)；返回 [{path, line, text}] 行级匹配。 何时不用: 只想按文件名 / 路径找用 glob_files；要读完整文件用 read_file；要做语义级代码检索用 code_search / lsp_skills；二进制或 >1MB 的文件会被自动跳过。 关键参数: pattern (必填, Python re); root (默认 '.'); path (可选, 精确文件/目录且优先于注入的 root); glob (默认 '**/*'); ignore_case (默认 False); max_matches (默认 100, 上限 500); max_files (默认 5000, 上限 20000)。默认跳过 node_modules、dist、build、coverage、虚拟环境和隐藏目录。 示例: grep_text({\\\"pattern\\\": \\\"def register_\\\", \\\"root\\\": \\\"runtime\\\", \\\"glob\\\": \\\"**/*.py\\\"})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"hash_text 用途: 对一段文本计算 blake2b (16 字节) 或 sha256 摘要；用于校验、去重 key、签名前缀等。 何时不用: 要校验文件内容用 read_file 取出后再哈希；需要 HMAC / 密钥派生用 ipython 跑 hashlib/hmac；想加密 (而非摘要) 不要用本工具。 关键参数: text (必填); algorithm (\\\"blake2b\\\" 默认 / \\\"sha256\\\")。 示例: hash_text({\\\"text\\\": \\\"abc\\\", \\\"algorithm\\\": \\\"sha256\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: hash_text\n      - generic: \"用途: 对一段文本计算 blake2b (16 字节) 或 sha256 摘要；用于校验、去重 key、签名前缀等。 何时不用: 要校验文件内容用 read_file 取出后再哈希；需要 HMAC / 密钥派生用 ipython 跑 hashlib/hmac；想加密 (而非摘要) 不要用本工具。 关键参数: text (必填); algorithm (\\\"blake2b\\\" 默认 / \\\"sha256\\\")。 示例: hash_text({\\\"text\\\": \\\"abc\\\", \\\"algorithm\\\": \\\"sha256\\\"})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"history_read Read the message transcript of one past conversation thread. Use after `history_search` gives you a thread_id. Args: {thread_id: string (required), limit?: int (default 50, max 100 — most recent N messages)}. Returns {thread_id, title, count, total_messages, messages: [{role, content, truncated}]}. Long messages are clipped; `truncated: true` marks them.\"':\n      - generic: history_read\n      - generic: \"Read the message transcript of one past conversation thread. Use after `history_search` gives you a thread_id. Args: {thread_id: string (required), limit?: int (default 50, max 100 — most recent N messages)}. Returns {thread_id, title, count, total_messages, messages: [{role, content, truncated}]}. Long messages are clipped; `truncated: true` marks them.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"history_search Search your PAST CONVERSATIONS (other threads) by keyword and/or date range. CALL THIS WHEN the user refers to something discussed ''before'', ''last time'', ''the other day'', or in a named past session — you cannot see other threads otherwise. Distinct from `recall`, which reads saved MEMORY.md facts; this reads the actual chat transcripts. Args: {query?: string (case-insensitive substring over title + message bodies; omit to list by date alone), start_date?: ''YYYY-MM-DD'' or ISO, end_date?: ''YYYY-MM-DD'' or ISO (inclusive), days_back?: int (shortcut for start_date = N days ago), limit?: int (default 20, max 100), include_current?: bool (default false — the thread you''re already in is excluded)}. Returns {count, threads: [{thread_id, title, snippet, created_at, updated_at, message_count}]}. Follow up with `history_read` on a thread_id to read the full transcript.\"':\n      - generic: history_search\n      - generic: \"Search your PAST CONVERSATIONS (other threads) by keyword and/or date range. CALL THIS WHEN the user refers to something discussed 'before', 'last time', 'the other day', or in a named past session — you cannot see other threads otherwise. Distinct from `recall`, which reads saved MEMORY.md facts; this reads the actual chat transcripts. Args: {query?: string (case-insensitive substring over title + message bodies; omit to list by date alone), start_date?: 'YYYY-MM-DD' or ISO, end_date?: 'YYYY-MM-DD' or ISO (inclusive), days_back?: int (shortcut for start_date = N days ago), limit?: int (default 20, max 100), include_current?: bool (default false — the thread you're already in is excluded)}. Returns {count, threads: [{thread_id, title, snippet, created_at, updated_at, message_count}]}. Follow up with `history_read` on a thread_id to read the full transcript.\"\n    - menuitem \"http-load-tester HTTP 阶梯式并发压测工具，自动执行多级并发压力测试，采集 p50/p90/p99 延迟百分位数，分析性能拐点（如延迟激增、吞吐饱和或错误率飙升），并输出结构化报告与最优并发建议。使用纯 Python 标准库，零外部依赖。当用户提及 HTTP 压测、基准测试、ab、wrk、并发测试、阶梯压测、延迟百分位、p99、拐点分析、性能测试、QPS、RPS 或容量规划等关键词或场景时触发。\":\n      - generic: http-load-tester\n      - generic: HTTP 阶梯式并发压测工具，自动执行多级并发压力测试，采集 p50/p90/p99 延迟百分位数，分析性能拐点（如延迟激增、吞吐饱和或错误率飙升），并输出结构化报告与最优并发建议。使用纯 Python 标准库，零外部依赖。当用户提及 HTTP 压测、基准测试、ab、wrk、并发测试、阶梯压测、延迟百分位、p99、拐点分析、性能测试、QPS、RPS 或容量规划等关键词或场景时触发。\n    - menuitem \"incident-retrospective 线上事故复盘与结构化 Blameless Postmortem 撰写工具，遵循 SRE 最佳实践。帮助用户撰写专业的事故复盘报告，通过六步 SOP 引导完成从时间线梳理、5 Whys 根因分析到制定 SMART 改进措施的全过程，输出格式化的复盘文档。当用户需要撰写事故复盘、进行根因分析（RCA）、创建 blameless postmortem、分析线上故障、制定改进措施（action items）或总结事故教训时触发，常见于提到 postmortem、事故复盘、故障分析、RCA、5 Whys、incident review、故障报告等关键词的场景。\":\n      - generic: incident-retrospective\n      - generic: 线上事故复盘与结构化 Blameless Postmortem 撰写工具，遵循 SRE 最佳实践。帮助用户撰写专业的事故复盘报告，通过六步 SOP 引导完成从时间线梳理、5 Whys 根因分析到制定 SMART 改进措施的全过程，输出格式化的复盘文档。当用户需要撰写事故复盘、进行根因分析（RCA）、创建 blameless postmortem、分析线上故障、制定改进措施（action items）或总结事故教训时触发，常见于提到 postmortem、事故复盘、故障分析、RCA、5 Whys、incident review、故障报告等关键词的场景。\n    - menuitem \"inspect_candidate_patch Inspect an isolated candidate patch previously returned by call_agent or tournament. Pass only candidate_sha256 from the worktree receipt. The host resolves the actual patch, baseline and project from its durable journal, checks every path and exact before/after state, and returns an inspection_id plus a bounded diff. This does not modify project files.\":\n      - generic: inspect_candidate_patch\n      - generic: Inspect an isolated candidate patch previously returned by call_agent or tournament. Pass only candidate_sha256 from the worktree receipt. The host resolves the actual patch, baseline and project from its durable journal, checks every path and exact before/after state, and returns an inspection_id plus a bounded diff. This does not modify project files.\n    - menuitem \"interface-design-lab 为模块生成多种截然不同的接口设计方案，通过并行探索产出多个接口签名、使用示例和封装说明，并详细对比其简洁性、通用性、深度与易用性。当用户需要设计API、探索接口方案、对比模块形态，或明确提及“设计两次”原则、并行设计、接口形态比较时触发。\":\n      - generic: interface-design-lab\n      - generic: 为模块生成多种截然不同的接口设计方案，通过并行探索产出多个接口签名、使用示例和封装说明，并详细对比其简洁性、通用性、深度与易用性。当用户需要设计API、探索接口方案、对比模块形态，或明确提及“设计两次”原则、并行设计、接口形态比较时触发。\n    - menuitem \"interview-simulator 模拟真实面试官进行追问训练，覆盖行为面试、技术面试和案例面试三大场景，每次训练包含3-5轮循序渐进的追问，并基于STAR框架对用户回答进行结构化诊断与优化，输出综合评分和改进建议。当用户希望练习面试、提及行为面试/技术面试/案例面试等关键词、或直接给出面试问题或回答内容时触发。\":\n      - generic: interview-simulator\n      - generic: 模拟真实面试官进行追问训练，覆盖行为面试、技术面试和案例面试三大场景，每次训练包含3-5轮循序渐进的追问，并基于STAR框架对用户回答进行结构化诊断与优化，输出综合评分和改进建议。当用户希望练习面试、提及行为面试/技术面试/案例面试等关键词、或直接给出面试问题或回答内容时触发。\n    - 'menuitem \"ipython 用途: 在带超时的子进程里跑一段 Python (当前解释器, 无 REPL 状态保留)；适合数据分析、临时计算、调用 numpy/pandas/json。 何时不用: 跑非 Python 命令用 exec_shell；只是数文本用 count_words；改文件用 edit_file 而不是写脚本绕路；要长跑用 background_exec / exec_shell(run_in_background=True)。 关键参数: code (必填, 完整 Python 片段, 用 print 才能拿到 stdout); cwd (可选); timeout_s (默认 60)。 示例: ipython({\\\"code\\\": \\\"import json; print(json.dumps({\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\": 1}))\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: ipython\n      - generic: \"用途: 在带超时的子进程里跑一段 Python (当前解释器, 无 REPL 状态保留)；适合数据分析、临时计算、调用 numpy/pandas/json。 何时不用: 跑非 Python 命令用 exec_shell；只是数文本用 count_words；改文件用 edit_file 而不是写脚本绕路；要长跑用 background_exec / exec_shell(run_in_background=True)。 关键参数: code (必填, 完整 Python 片段, 用 print 才能拿到 stdout); cwd (可选); timeout_s (默认 60)。 示例: ipython({\\\"code\\\": \\\"import json; print(json.dumps({\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\": 1}))\\\"})\"\n    - menuitem \"keyboard_press Press a key or key combo · keys=['enter'] or ['ctrl','c'].\":\n      - generic: keyboard_press\n      - generic: Press a key or key combo · keys=['enter'] or ['ctrl','c'].\n    - menuitem \"keyboard_type Type text via keyboard (len ≤ 10k, with per-char interval).\":\n      - generic: keyboard_type\n      - generic: Type text via keyboard (len ≤ 10k, with per-char interval).\n    - 'menuitem \"kill_background_exec Stop a command started by `background_exec`.\"':\n      - generic: kill_background_exec\n      - generic: \"Stop a command started by `background_exec`.\"\n    - menuitem \"kill_shell Alias for kill_background_exec. Stop a command started by exec_shell(run_in_background=True) or background_exec.\":\n      - generic: kill_shell\n      - generic: Alias for kill_background_exec. Stop a command started by exec_shell(run_in_background=True) or background_exec.\n    - menuitem \"kubectl Execute kubectl commands to manage Kubernetes clusters — query pods and deployments, deploy applications, debug containers with logs and exec, update configurations, and monitor cluster health. Use when working with Kubernetes, asking for pod status, container logs, deployment updates, cluster diagnostics, or any kubectl operation.\":\n      - generic: kubectl\n      - generic: Execute kubectl commands to manage Kubernetes clusters — query pods and deployments, deploy applications, debug containers with logs and exec, update configurations, and monitor cluster health. Use when working with Kubernetes, asking for pod status, container logs, deployment updates, cluster diagnostics, or any kubectl operation.\n    - menuitem \"landing-page-scaffold Generate a self-contained landing page HTML prototype with five standard sections (Hero → Social Proof → Features → Pricing → CTA), outputting a single inlined HTML file ready to preview in any browser. Triggered when the user asks to build, generate, or scaffold a landing page, wireframe, or marketing page prototype, or mentions specific sections like hero, pricing, or CTA.\":\n      - generic: landing-page-scaffold\n      - generic: Generate a self-contained landing page HTML prototype with five standard sections (Hero → Social Proof → Features → Pricing → CTA), outputting a single inlined HTML file ready to preview in any browser. Triggered when the user asks to build, generate, or scaffold a landing page, wireframe, or marketing page prototype, or mentions specific sections like hero, pricing, or CTA.\n    - menuitem:\n      - generic: learn_skill_from_text\n      - generic: \"Learn a reusable output template from a high-quality sample. The agent feeds in text (e.g. a tech-comparison report copy-pasted from a PDF, or a slide outline), the LLM extracts the structural + stylistic DNA, and the result is persisted at agents/<your_id>/skills/<name>.md so YOU (or a future session) can `apply_skill(name, ...)` to produce same-shape outputs for a different topic. Args: {name: short slug like 'tech-comparison-report', sample_text: the doc text (≤ 8K chars), sample_source?: where it came from, golden_samples?: list of 3+ alternate user_requests (or pipe-separated string 'a|b|c') — if given, template is TESTED against them before persisting and rejected if < 2/3 preserve the template's H2 structure; golden_pass_threshold?: float (default 0.66), model?: override LLM}. EXPENSIVE · single LLM call (~3-5¢ haiku) per learn, +N more calls if golden_samples is provided.\"\n    - menuitem \"legal-contract-gen 通过交互式问答生成常用法律文书初稿，支持NDA（保密协议）、服务协议、隐私政策、合作框架协议等类型。当用户提到NDA、保密协议、服务协议、隐私政策、合同模板、法律文书、合作协议，或相应的英文术语（如terms of service、privacy policy、service agreement、non-disclosure agreement、contract template、legal document）时触发。\":\n      - generic: legal-contract-gen\n      - generic: 通过交互式问答生成常用法律文书初稿，支持NDA（保密协议）、服务协议、隐私政策、合作框架协议等类型。当用户提到NDA、保密协议、服务协议、隐私政策、合同模板、法律文书、合作协议，或相应的英文术语（如terms of service、privacy policy、service agreement、non-disclosure agreement、contract template、legal document）时触发。\n    - menuitem \"legal-risk-analyzer 法律风险评估助手，基于“严重性 × 发生概率”的框架评估法律风险，提供风险评分、等级（绿/黄/橙/红）及具体行动建议（从接受监控到上报法务负责人或聘请外部律师）。适用于用户询问合同风险、交易风险、问题分级、或是否需要上报高级法务/外部律师等场景，当用户提及风险评估、风险等级、法律风险分析或类似关键词时触发。\":\n      - generic: legal-risk-analyzer\n      - generic: 法律风险评估助手，基于“严重性 × 发生概率”的框架评估法律风险，提供风险评分、等级（绿/黄/橙/红）及具体行动建议（从接受监控到上报法务负责人或聘请外部律师）。适用于用户询问合同风险、交易风险、问题分级、或是否需要上报高级法务/外部律师等场景，当用户提及风险评估、风险等级、法律风险分析或类似关键词时触发。\n    - menuitem \"lint_check Run linter (auto-detects ruff/eslint). Returns diagnostics plus safe-fix diff; pass fix=true to apply safe fixes.\":\n      - generic: lint_check\n      - generic: Run linter (auto-detects ruff/eslint). Returns diagnostics plus safe-fix diff; pass fix=true to apply safe fixes.\n    - 'menuitem \"list_cwd 用途: 非递归列出一个目录的直接子项（隐藏项已过滤）；快速浏览结构。 何时不用: 需要多层深度用 tree；按 glob 过滤用 glob_files；要文件元数据用 file_stats；按内容找用 grep_text。 关键参数: path (默认 \\\".\\\"); cwd (相对路径基准, 可选)。 示例: list_cwd({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/execution/suckers\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: list_cwd\n      - generic: \"用途: 非递归列出一个目录的直接子项（隐藏项已过滤）；快速浏览结构。 何时不用: 需要多层深度用 tree；按 glob 过滤用 glob_files；要文件元数据用 file_stats；按内容找用 grep_text。 关键参数: path (默认 \\\".\\\"); cwd (相对路径基准, 可选)。 示例: list_cwd({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/execution/suckers\\\"})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"list_learned_skills List skills you''ve previously learned via `learn_skill_from_text`. Returns {ok, count, skills:[{name, description, when_to_use, sample_source, learned_at, filename, size_bytes}]}. Use this to discover what shapes you can already reproduce before deciding to learn a new one.\"':\n      - generic: list_learned_skills\n      - generic: \"List skills you've previously learned via `learn_skill_from_text`. Returns {ok, count, skills:[{name, description, when_to_use, sample_source, learned_at, filename, size_bytes}]}. Use this to discover what shapes you can already reproduce before deciding to learn a new one.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"list_scheduled_tasks List scheduled tasks owned by the current authenticated tenant and actor (or legacy local tasks in local mode). Returns {ok, tasks: [{task_id, cron_expression, creator_actor, next_run_at, fire_at, recurring, prompt, last_run, last_status}], count}.\"':\n      - generic: list_scheduled_tasks\n      - generic: \"List scheduled tasks owned by the current authenticated tenant and actor (or legacy local tasks in local mode). Returns {ok, tasks: [{task_id, cron_expression, creator_actor, next_run_at, fire_at, recurring, prompt, last_run, last_status}], count}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"list_soul_history List the most recent SOUL.md snapshots (newest first). Each `update_soul` and `revert_soul` leaves a snapshot here. Use this to see what changed when before deciding to roll back. Args: {limit?: int, default 10}. Returns {ok, count, snapshots: [{filename, size_bytes, mtime_iso}, ...]}.\"':\n      - generic: list_soul_history\n      - generic: \"List the most recent SOUL.md snapshots (newest first). Each `update_soul` and `revert_soul` leaves a snapshot here. Use this to see what changed when before deciding to roll back. Args: {limit?: int, default 10}. Returns {ok, count, snapshots: [{filename, size_bytes, mtime_iso}, ...]}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"live_browser_click Click an element on the **current active browser tab** by CSS selector. Octopus prefers its desktop webview and uses the signed-in Chrome relay when no desktop webview is active. Args: {selector: CSS selector, e.g. ''button[type=submit]'' or ''#login''}. Returns {ok, tag, text, error?}. Use `browser_extract` after click to read the resulting page.\"':\n      - generic: live_browser_click\n      - generic: \"Click an element on the **current active browser tab** by CSS selector. Octopus prefers its desktop webview and uses the signed-in Chrome relay when no desktop webview is active. Args: {selector: CSS selector, e.g. 'button[type=submit]' or '#login'}. Returns {ok, tag, text, error?}. Use `browser_extract` after click to read the resulting page.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"live_browser_current_url Return the URL and title of the current active browser tab. Cheap probe — use to verify navigation succeeded or to remember where you are without re-reading content. Args: {} (none). Returns {ok, url, title, error?}.\"':\n      - generic: live_browser_current_url\n      - generic: \"Return the URL and title of the current active browser tab. Cheap probe — use to verify navigation succeeded or to remember where you are without re-reading content. Args: {} (none). Returns {ok, url, title, error?}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"live_browser_execute_js Run arbitrary JavaScript in the current page''s main world. Escape hatch for things not covered by other primitives. Returns {ok, result, error?} where `result` is the JS expression''s return value (must be JSON-serializable). Args: {code: JavaScript expression or IIFE}. Examples: - code=''document.querySelectorAll(\\\"a\\\").length'' → count links - code=''[...document.querySelectorAll(\\\"h1\\\")].map(el=>el.innerText)'' → all H1 text USE WITH CAUTION · arbitrary JS can break the page.\"':\n      - generic: live_browser_execute_js\n      - generic: \"Run arbitrary JavaScript in the current page's main world. Escape hatch for things not covered by other primitives. Returns {ok, result, error?} where `result` is the JS expression's return value (must be JSON-serializable). Args: {code: JavaScript expression or IIFE}. Examples: - code='document.querySelectorAll(\\\"a\\\").length' → count links - code='[...document.querySelectorAll(\\\"h1\\\")].map(el=>el.innerText)' → all H1 text USE WITH CAUTION · arbitrary JS can break the page.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"live_browser_extract Read the current page''s text content (article body or main, fall back to body). Excludes scripts/styles/iframes. Truncated to 20K chars. Args: {} (none). Returns {ok, url, title, text, truncated, textLength, error?}. Use this as the agent''s primary ''see the page'' primitive — cheap, fast, no LLM-vision cost.\"':\n      - generic: live_browser_extract\n      - generic: \"Read the current page's text content (article body or main, fall back to body). Excludes scripts/styles/iframes. Truncated to 20K chars. Args: {} (none). Returns {ok, url, title, text, truncated, textLength, error?}. Use this as the agent's primary 'see the page' primitive — cheap, fast, no LLM-vision cost.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"live_browser_find Find text on the current active browser tab and return match snippets. Args: {text/query, case_sensitive?, max_results?, context_chars?}. Returns {ok, url, title, count, matches, error?}.\"':\n      - generic: live_browser_find\n      - generic: \"Find text on the current active browser tab and return match snippets. Args: {text/query, case_sensitive?, max_results?, context_chars?}. Returns {ok, url, title, count, matches, error?}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"live_browser_navigate Load a new URL in the current active tab. Args: {url: full https://... URL}. Returns {ok, url, error?}. Follow with `browser_extract` or `browser_wait` to confirm load.\"':\n      - generic: live_browser_navigate\n      - generic: \"Load a new URL in the current active tab. Args: {url: full https://... URL}. Returns {ok, url, error?}. Follow with `browser_extract` or `browser_wait` to confirm load.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"live_browser_screenshot Capture a screenshot of the current active tab as a base64 PNG data URL. EXPENSIVE in context (data URL ~hundreds of KB chars). Prefer `browser_extract` for text-based reasoning. Use screenshot only when visual layout / image content actually matters. Args: {} (none). Returns {ok, dataUrl, width, height, error?}.\"':\n      - generic: live_browser_screenshot\n      - generic: \"Capture a screenshot of the current active tab as a base64 PNG data URL. EXPENSIVE in context (data URL ~hundreds of KB chars). Prefer `browser_extract` for text-based reasoning. Use screenshot only when visual layout / image content actually matters. Args: {} (none). Returns {ok, dataUrl, width, height, error?}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"live_browser_scroll Scroll the current page. Two modes: - {selector: CSS} · scroll the element into view (smooth) - {delta_y: pixels} · scroll the page by N pixels (positive=down) Returns {ok, y?, error?}.\"':\n      - generic: live_browser_scroll\n      - generic: \"Scroll the current page. Two modes: - {selector: CSS} · scroll the element into view (smooth) - {delta_y: pixels} · scroll the page by N pixels (positive=down) Returns {ok, y?, error?}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"live_browser_state Return the current active browser tab state: URL, title, viewport, scroll, and visible links/buttons/inputs/headings. Args: {max_items?}.\"':\n      - generic: live_browser_state\n      - generic: \"Return the current active browser tab state: URL, title, viewport, scroll, and visible links/buttons/inputs/headings. Args: {max_items?}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"live_browser_type Type text into an input/textarea on the current active browser tab. Args: {selector: CSS, text: string to type, clear?: bool (default false; true clears existing first)}. Triggers `input` and `change` events so React/Vue forms see the change. Returns {ok, value, error?}.\"':\n      - generic: live_browser_type\n      - generic: \"Type text into an input/textarea on the current active browser tab. Args: {selector: CSS, text: string to type, clear?: bool (default false; true clears existing first)}. Triggers `input` and `change` events so React/Vue forms see the change. Returns {ok, value, error?}.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"live_browser_wait Poll for a CSS selector to appear (and be visible) on the current page. Use after navigation or click when the next step needs an element that loads async. Args: {selector: CSS, timeout?: ms (default 10000)}. Returns {ok, elapsed, error?}.\"':\n      - generic: live_browser_wait\n      - generic: \"Poll for a CSS selector to appear (and be visible) on the current page. Use after navigation or click when the next step needs an element that loads async. Args: {selector: CSS, timeout?: ms (default 10000)}. Returns {ok, elapsed, error?}.\"\n    - menuitem \"localization-toolkit This skill should be used when setting up, auditing, or enforcing internationalization/localization in UI codebases (React/TS, i18next or similar, JSON locales), including installing/configuring the i18n framework, replacing hard-coded strings, ensuring en-US/zh-CN coverage, mapping error codes to localized messages, and validating key parity, pluralization, and formatting.\":\n      - generic: localization-toolkit\n      - generic: This skill should be used when setting up, auditing, or enforcing internationalization/localization in UI codebases (React/TS, i18next or similar, JSON locales), including installing/configuring the i18n framework, replacing hard-coded strings, ensuring en-US/zh-CN coverage, mapping error codes to localized messages, and validating key parity, pluralization, and formatting.\n    - menuitem \"log-diagnostic 分析日志文件的错误模式，支持JSON、syslog、Nginx等常见格式，自动检测并输出错误聚类、频率统计和时间分布报告，用于排查问题、定位高发时段。当用户上传.log文件并要求排查错误、分析错误分布、定位高发时段，或提及错误统计、日志分析等关键词时触发。\":\n      - generic: log-diagnostic\n      - generic: 分析日志文件的错误模式，支持JSON、syslog、Nginx等常见格式，自动检测并输出错误聚类、频率统计和时间分布报告，用于排查问题、定位高发时段。当用户上传.log文件并要求排查错误、分析错误分布、定位高发时段，或提及错误统计、日志分析等关键词时触发。\n    - 'menuitem \"lsp_definition 用途: 通过 LSP 跳转到符号定义 (file/line/column → 真正的定义位置)，比 code_search 的正则更精确，能跨文件跨包解析。 何时不用: 不知道符号在哪一行/哪一列时先用 code_search/grep 定位坐标；只想看文件结构用 lsp_document_symbols；项目里没装对应语言的 language server 时会返回 dependency_missing。 关键参数: path (必填, 文件路径)；line (必填, 1-indexed 行号)；column (必填, 1-indexed 列号, 通常指向标识符的第一个字符)。 示例: lsp_definition({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/foo.py\\\", \\\"line\\\": 42, \\\"column\\\": 11})\"':\n      - generic: lsp_definition\n      - generic: \"用途: 通过 LSP 跳转到符号定义 (file/line/column → 真正的定义位置)，比 code_search 的正则更精确，能跨文件跨包解析。 何时不用: 不知道符号在哪一行/哪一列时先用 code_search/grep 定位坐标；只想看文件结构用 lsp_document_symbols；项目里没装对应语言的 language server 时会返回 dependency_missing。 关键参数: path (必填, 文件路径)；line (必填, 1-indexed 行号)；column (必填, 1-indexed 列号, 通常指向标识符的第一个字符)。 示例: lsp_definition({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/foo.py\\\", \\\"line\\\": 42, \\\"column\\\": 11})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"lsp_document_symbols 用途: 通过 LSP 列出一个文件里所有符号 (类、函数、方法、变量) 及其行列坐标和容器关系，相当于 IDE 大纲面板。 何时不用: 只想找一个具体名字用 code_search 或 lsp_definition；想跨文件查询用 code_search；没装 language server 时回 dependency_missing。 关键参数: path (必填, 要分析的文件路径)。 示例: lsp_document_symbols({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/foo.py\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: lsp_document_symbols\n      - generic: \"用途: 通过 LSP 列出一个文件里所有符号 (类、函数、方法、变量) 及其行列坐标和容器关系，相当于 IDE 大纲面板。 何时不用: 只想找一个具体名字用 code_search 或 lsp_definition；想跨文件查询用 code_search；没装 language server 时回 dependency_missing。 关键参数: path (必填, 要分析的文件路径)。 示例: lsp_document_symbols({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/foo.py\\\"})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"lsp_hover 用途: 通过 LSP 获取某个位置的悬停信息 (类型签名、docstring、推断的表达式类型)，相当于 IDE 里把鼠标悬停的效果。 何时不用: 想读整个文件用 read_file；想列出文件里所有符号用 lsp_document_symbols；没装 language server 时回 dependency_missing。 关键参数: path (必填)；line (必填, 1-indexed)；column (必填, 1-indexed, 指向标识符)。 示例: lsp_hover({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/foo.py\\\", \\\"line\\\": 42, \\\"column\\\": 11})\"':\n      - generic: lsp_hover\n      - generic: \"用途: 通过 LSP 获取某个位置的悬停信息 (类型签名、docstring、推断的表达式类型)，相当于 IDE 里把鼠标悬停的效果。 何时不用: 想读整个文件用 read_file；想列出文件里所有符号用 lsp_document_symbols；没装 language server 时回 dependency_missing。 关键参数: path (必填)；line (必填, 1-indexed)；column (必填, 1-indexed, 指向标识符)。 示例: lsp_hover({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/foo.py\\\", \\\"line\\\": 42, \\\"column\\\": 11})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"lsp_references 用途: 通过 LSP 列出符号的所有引用/使用点 (谁调用了 foo / 谁读写了这个变量)，跨文件查找比 code_search 更准。 何时不用: 只想看一个文件内的 grep 结果用 code_search；不知道坐标时先 code_search 找到再 lsp_references；没安装 language server 时回 dependency_missing。 关键参数: path (必填)；line (必填, 1-indexed)；column (必填, 1-indexed)；include_declaration (可选, 默认 True, 结果是否包含定义位置本身)。 示例: lsp_references({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/foo.py\\\", \\\"line\\\": 42, \\\"column\\\": 11, \\\"include_declaration\\\": false})\"':\n      - generic: lsp_references\n      - generic: \"用途: 通过 LSP 列出符号的所有引用/使用点 (谁调用了 foo / 谁读写了这个变量)，跨文件查找比 code_search 更准。 何时不用: 只想看一个文件内的 grep 结果用 code_search；不知道坐标时先 code_search 找到再 lsp_references；没安装 language server 时回 dependency_missing。 关键参数: path (必填)；line (必填, 1-indexed)；column (必填, 1-indexed)；include_declaration (可选, 默认 True, 结果是否包含定义位置本身)。 示例: lsp_references({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/foo.py\\\", \\\"line\\\": 42, \\\"column\\\": 11, \\\"include_declaration\\\": false})\"\n    - menuitem \"mouse_click Click at (x,y) · button=left|right|middle · clicks ≤ 5 · bounds-checked.\":\n      - generic: mouse_click\n      - generic: Click at (x,y) · button=left|right|middle · clicks ≤ 5 · bounds-checked.\n    - 'menuitem \"mouse_move Smoothly move cursor to (x,y) over `duration` seconds.\"':\n      - generic: mouse_move\n      - generic: \"Smoothly move cursor to (x,y) over `duration` seconds.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"multi_edit_file 用途: 一次调用对同一文件原子化应用多个精确替换 (按 edits 顺序累积)；适合重构 / 同时改多处。任一编辑失败整批回滚。 何时不用: 只改一处用 edit_file；不同文件分别处理；要一行 find/replace 全文扫荡用 edit_text_file；要新建文件用 write_text_file。 关键参数: path (必填); edits (必填, list[{old_string, new_string, replace_all?}], 顺序敏感, 默认每条要求唯一)。 示例: multi_edit_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"a.py\\\", \\\"edits\\\": [{\\\"old_string\\\": \\\"v1\\\", \\\"new_string\\\": \\\"v2\\\"}, {\\\"old_string\\\": \\\"x\\\", \\\"new_string\\\": \\\"y\\\", \\\"replace_all\\\": true}]})\"':\n      - generic: multi_edit_file\n      - generic: \"用途: 一次调用对同一文件原子化应用多个精确替换 (按 edits 顺序累积)；适合重构 / 同时改多处。任一编辑失败整批回滚。 何时不用: 只改一处用 edit_file；不同文件分别处理；要一行 find/replace 全文扫荡用 edit_text_file；要新建文件用 write_text_file。 关键参数: path (必填); edits (必填, list[{old_string, new_string, replace_all?}], 顺序敏感, 默认每条要求唯一)。 示例: multi_edit_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"a.py\\\", \\\"edits\\\": [{\\\"old_string\\\": \\\"v1\\\", \\\"new_string\\\": \\\"v2\\\"}, {\\\"old_string\\\": \\\"x\\\", \\\"new_string\\\": \\\"y\\\", \\\"replace_all\\\": true}]})\"\n    - menuitem \"mx2025.recent_messages 读取本机萌侠连接器已采集的最新消息。参数:limit 可选(1-500,默认100),query 可选(按老师名或正文搜索),room_id 可选(限定对话)。返回内容含老师/对话标题、消息正文、发布时间、消息类型和是否已同步云端。适用于分析老师观点、调研纪要、小作文、竞价观点和最近消息。\":\n      - generic: mx2025.recent_messages\n      - generic: 读取本机萌侠连接器已采集的最新消息。参数:limit 可选(1-500,默认100),query 可选(按老师名或正文搜索),room_id 可选(限定对话)。返回内容含老师/对话标题、消息正文、发布时间、消息类型和是否已同步云端。适用于分析老师观点、调研纪要、小作文、竞价观点和最近消息。\n    - 'menuitem \"narrative_studio.continuity Check Narrative Studio candidates for timeline, character-state, world-rule, relationship, and foreshadow continuity against cited project sources. # Continuity review Compare the target candidate with the branch''s source-cited context pack. Check chronology, identity, location, knowledge, inventory, relationships, promises, world rules, planted clues, and state transitions. Separate a sourced contradiction from an inference or an unresolved question, and include the relevant source refs in every finding. Return a candidate review or proposed state-change record only. Do not rewrite source facts as canon, vote on a review, clear a blocker, or create a CanonCommit. If context is truncated or lacks the necessary source, state that limitation rather than claiming certainty.\"':\n      - generic: narrative_studio.continuity\n      - generic: \"Check Narrative Studio candidates for timeline, character-state, world-rule, relationship, and foreshadow continuity against cited project sources. # Continuity review Compare the target candidate with the branch's source-cited context pack. Check chronology, identity, location, knowledge, inventory, relationships, promises, world rules, planted clues, and state transitions. Separate a sourced contradiction from an inference or an unresolved question, and include the relevant source refs in every finding. Return a candidate review or proposed state-change record only. Do not rewrite source facts as canon, vote on a review, clear a blocker, or create a CanonCommit. If context is truncated or lacks the necessary source, state that limitation rather than claiming certainty.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"narrative_studio.editorial_readiness Prepare an evidence-based editorial recommendation for a Narrative Studio candidate without exercising human canon-governance authority. # Canon readiness review Assess whether a candidate is ready for human governance. Summarize scope, revision, supporting source refs, continuity findings, unresolved blockers, and a recommendation of `ready_for_human_review`, `revise`, or `insufficient_evidence`. Distinguish editorial preference from a factual or policy blocker. This skill has no governance authority. It must not submit or alter votes, mark review requests resolved, remove blockers, create a CanonCommit, or describe a candidate as canon. Only an authenticated human governance path with explicit confirmation may perform those actions.\"':\n      - generic: narrative_studio.editorial_readiness\n      - generic: \"Prepare an evidence-based editorial recommendation for a Narrative Studio candidate without exercising human canon-governance authority. # Canon readiness review Assess whether a candidate is ready for human governance. Summarize scope, revision, supporting source refs, continuity findings, unresolved blockers, and a recommendation of `ready_for_human_review`, `revise`, or `insufficient_evidence`. Distinguish editorial preference from a factual or policy blocker. This skill has no governance authority. It must not submit or alter votes, mark review requests resolved, remove blockers, create a CanonCommit, or describe a candidate as canon. Only an authenticated human governance path with explicit confirmation may perform those actions.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"narrative_studio.narrative_authoring Develop outlines, scenes, and chapters in Narrative Studio when the requested output must remain a reviewable candidate. # Narrative authoring Use the project''s selected branch and a bounded context pack as the source of truth. Preserve the requested voice, point of view, tense, language, and target length. Treat world facts and earlier chapter state as constraints, and cite their source refs in the candidate''s supporting notes when available. Create or revise only candidate artifacts. Never label prose as approved canon, cast governance votes, resolve blocking reviews, or create a CanonCommit. Surface contradictions or missing evidence for human review instead of silently inventing a resolution.\"':\n      - generic: narrative_studio.narrative_authoring\n      - generic: \"Develop outlines, scenes, and chapters in Narrative Studio when the requested output must remain a reviewable candidate. # Narrative authoring Use the project's selected branch and a bounded context pack as the source of truth. Preserve the requested voice, point of view, tense, language, and target length. Treat world facts and earlier chapter state as constraints, and cite their source refs in the candidate's supporting notes when available. Create or revise only candidate artifacts. Never label prose as approved canon, cast governance votes, resolve blocking reviews, or create a CanonCommit. Surface contradictions or missing evidence for human review instead of silently inventing a resolution.\"\n    - menuitem \"narrative_studio.project_create 创建一个叙事项目和默认 main 候选分支。参数 title 必填；可选 id、premise、language=zh|en|bilingual。此技能不创建或晋升正典。\":\n      - generic: narrative_studio.project_create\n      - generic: 创建一个叙事项目和默认 main 候选分支。参数 title 必填；可选 id、premise、language=zh|en|bilingual。此技能不创建或晋升正典。\n    - 'menuitem \"note_user Record an unverified observation about a user trait or preference (communication style, skill level, language preference, recurring patterns). CALL THIS WHEN you learn something about the user that should shape how you respond going forward — e.g. ''prefers Chinese'', ''wants terse answers'', ''is a senior engineer'', ''doesn''t know Rust''. Args: {trait: string}. Distinct from `remember` — that''s for facts about the world / project, this is for observations about the user. Current explicit user instructions take precedence; this tool does not confirm inferred preferences.\"':\n      - generic: note_user\n      - generic: \"Record an unverified observation about a user trait or preference (communication style, skill level, language preference, recurring patterns). CALL THIS WHEN you learn something about the user that should shape how you respond going forward — e.g. 'prefers Chinese', 'wants terse answers', 'is a senior engineer', 'doesn't know Rust'. Args: {trait: string}. Distinct from `remember` — that's for facts about the world / project, this is for observations about the user. Current explicit user instructions take precedence; this tool does not confirm inferred preferences.\"\n    - menuitem \"okr-planner OKR 制定/拆解/复盘教练。当用户提到以下场景时触发：OKR、目标管理、关键结果、OKR制定、OKR拆解、OKR复盘、OKR检查、OKR对齐、季度目标、objectives and key results、目标拆解、KR制定、OKR评分、OKR改进。即使用户只是说'帮我写个OKR''这个OKR写得好不好''帮我复盘一下这个季度的OKR''目标怎么拆解'，也应触发。\":\n      - generic: okr-planner\n      - generic: OKR 制定/拆解/复盘教练。当用户提到以下场景时触发：OKR、目标管理、关键结果、OKR制定、OKR拆解、OKR复盘、OKR检查、OKR对齐、季度目标、objectives and key results、目标拆解、KR制定、OKR评分、OKR改进。即使用户只是说'帮我写个OKR''这个OKR写得好不好''帮我复盘一下这个季度的OKR''目标怎么拆解'，也应触发。\n    - menuitem \"paper_trading.quote 查询模拟炒股(paper_trading)插件里某个 A 股的当前模拟报价(现价/涨跌幅/昨收)。参数 code 必填,如 '600519'。纯模拟数据,不连真实行情。\":\n      - generic: paper_trading.quote\n      - generic: 查询模拟炒股(paper_trading)插件里某个 A 股的当前模拟报价(现价/涨跌幅/昨收)。参数 code 必填,如 '600519'。纯模拟数据,不连真实行情。\n    - 'menuitem \"paper-writing End-to-end academic paper creation — outline design, structured content writing, review, and assembly. Covers survey papers, empirical research, technical papers, case studies, literature reviews, and any formal academic writing requiring methodology sections, contribution positioning, and rigorous citation. Outputs are delivered in Markdown (`.md`) format. Do NOT use for: industry reports, consulting deliverables, policy briefs (use report-writing).\"':\n      - generic: paper-writing\n      - generic: \"End-to-end academic paper creation — outline design, structured content writing, review, and assembly. Covers survey papers, empirical research, technical papers, case studies, literature reviews, and any formal academic writing requiring methodology sections, contribution positioning, and rigorous citation. Outputs are delivered in Markdown (`.md`) format. Do NOT use for: industry reports, consulting deliverables, policy briefs (use report-writing).\"\n    - menuitem \"pipeline-blueprint Provide CI/CD best practices and pipeline templates for GitHub Actions and GitLab CI, recommending configurations based on project type (frontend, backend, fullstack, library, monorepo, mobile). Trigger when users ask about setting up CI/CD, automating builds, improving pipelines, or mention keywords like GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, pipeline templates, or deployment automation.\":\n      - generic: pipeline-blueprint\n      - generic: Provide CI/CD best practices and pipeline templates for GitHub Actions and GitLab CI, recommending configurations based on project type (frontend, backend, fullstack, library, monorepo, mobile). Trigger when users ask about setting up CI/CD, automating builds, improving pipelines, or mention keywords like GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, pipeline templates, or deployment automation.\n    - 'menuitem \"platform_collect Run up to 50 queries and 100 URL reads in one bounded collection. Persists JSON or Markdown under ~/.octopus/data/reach/collections by default. Args: platform, queries, urls, max_results, output_path, output_format, use_browser. Use schedule_task with a prompt calling platform_collect for recurring monitoring.\"':\n      - generic: platform_collect\n      - generic: \"Run up to 50 queries and 100 URL reads in one bounded collection. Persists JSON or Markdown under ~/.octopus/data/reach/collections by default. Args: platform, queries, urls, max_results, output_path, output_format, use_browser. Use schedule_task with a prompt calling platform_collect for recurring monitoring.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"platform_monitor Schedule recurring platform_collect runs in Octopus'' existing cron store. Args: platform, queries, cron_expression, max_results, output_format, name, channel_id and thread_id. The result can be managed with list_scheduled_tasks and cancel_scheduled_task.\"':\n      - generic: platform_monitor\n      - generic: \"Schedule recurring platform_collect runs in Octopus' existing cron store. Args: platform, queries, cron_expression, max_results, output_format, name, channel_id and thread_id. The result can be managed with list_scheduled_tasks and cancel_scheduled_task.\"\n    - menuitem \"platform_read Read a URL using a platform-specific adapter. Public GitHub repositories, GitHub repositories/issues/pull requests, YouTube metadata/transcripts, Bilibili videos and RSS feeds are read directly. Reddit, X and Xiaohongshu return an explicit browser-session handoff when login is needed.\":\n      - generic: platform_read\n      - generic: Read a URL using a platform-specific adapter. Public GitHub repositories, GitHub repositories/issues/pull requests, YouTube metadata/transcripts, Bilibili videos and RSS feeds are read directly. Reddit, X and Xiaohongshu return an explicit browser-session handoff when login is needed.\n    - 'menuitem \"platform_search Search one platform through Octopus native adapters. Platforms: web, github, youtube, bilibili, reddit, x, xiaohongshu, douyin, toutiao and doubao. Uses public APIs where available and SearXNG site routing otherwise. Args: platform, query, max_results.\"':\n      - generic: platform_search\n      - generic: \"Search one platform through Octopus native adapters. Platforms: web, github, youtube, bilibili, reddit, x, xiaohongshu, douyin, toutiao and doubao. Uses public APIs where available and SearXNG site routing otherwise. Args: platform, query, max_results.\"\n    - menuitem \"pricing-advisor 设计与优化SaaS产品的定价体系，包括套餐结构、价值指标、定价页面及涨价策略，输出具体的定价方案与实施建议。当用户需要从零搭建定价模型、重构现有定价、规划涨价路径、或提升定价页转化率时触发，例如询问“SaaS如何定价”、“优化定价套餐”、“设计涨价策略”或提及“定价模型”、“价值指标”、“转化率”等关键词。\":\n      - generic: pricing-advisor\n      - generic: 设计与优化SaaS产品的定价体系，包括套餐结构、价值指标、定价页面及涨价策略，输出具体的定价方案与实施建议。当用户需要从零搭建定价模型、重构现有定价、规划涨价路径、或提升定价页转化率时触发，例如询问“SaaS如何定价”、“优化定价套餐”、“设计涨价策略”或提及“定价模型”、“价值指标”、“转化率”等关键词。\n    - menuitem \"product-spec-writer Transform one-line product ideas into complete PRD documents with user stories, feature lists, MoSCoW prioritization, and acceptance criteria. Trigger when users ask to 'write a PRD', 'turn this idea into a spec', 'flesh out requirements', or mention product requirements, user stories, feature breakdowns, or acceptance criteria.\":\n      - generic: product-spec-writer\n      - generic: Transform one-line product ideas into complete PRD documents with user stories, feature lists, MoSCoW prioritization, and acceptance criteria. Trigger when users ask to 'write a PRD', 'turn this idea into a spec', 'flesh out requirements', or mention product requirements, user stories, feature breakdowns, or acceptance criteria.\n    - menuitem \"project-sizing-guide Software project effort estimation assistant. Outputs three-point estimates (optimistic/most-likely/pessimistic values with confidence intervals), T-shirt sizes, or Function Point Analysis (FPA) counts. Triggered when users ask 'how long will this feature take,' need to assess project workload, perform PERT estimation, T-shirt sizing, FPA, sprint planning, or quote-based effort breakdowns.\":\n      - generic: project-sizing-guide\n      - generic: Software project effort estimation assistant. Outputs three-point estimates (optimistic/most-likely/pessimistic values with confidence intervals), T-shirt sizes, or Function Point Analysis (FPA) counts. Triggered when users ask 'how long will this feature take,' need to assess project workload, perform PERT estimation, T-shirt sizing, FPA, sprint planning, or quote-based effort breakdowns.\n    - menuitem \"py-perf-analyzer 定位 Python 脚本的性能瓶颈，集成 cProfile、tracemalloc 和 line_profiler，一键执行 CPU 热点函数、内存分配或逐行耗时分析，并可输出 JSON 报告。当用户提到优化脚本、分析性能、定位 CPU 或内存热点、进行逐行分析，或询问代码为什么慢、如何加速、内存泄漏等问题时触发。\":\n      - generic: py-perf-analyzer\n      - generic: 定位 Python 脚本的性能瓶颈，集成 cProfile、tracemalloc 和 line_profiler，一键执行 CPU 热点函数、内存分配或逐行耗时分析，并可输出 JSON 报告。当用户提到优化脚本、分析性能、定位 CPU 或内存热点、进行逐行分析，或询问代码为什么慢、如何加速、内存泄漏等问题时触发。\n    - menuitem \"query_capability Return the package-level details for one plugin or skill pack, including registered actions, child skills, MCP servers, and when-to-use guidance.\":\n      - generic: query_capability\n      - generic: Return the package-level details for one plugin or skill pack, including registered actions, child skills, MCP servers, and when-to-use guidance.\n    - 'menuitem \"query_skill 用途: 当 catalog 里的简短 summary 不够用时，按名字拉一个已注册 skill 的完整元数据 (description / 参数契约 / affinity / 是否启用)；调不熟的工具前先查一查。 何时不用: 列出全部 skill 不要用本工具 (走 catalog / registry.list)；要执行 skill 直接调用对应工具名，不要先 query 再调 (浪费 token)；skill 不存在会返回 ok=false。 关键参数: name (必填, 已注册的 skill 名)。 示例: query_skill({\\\"name\\\": \\\"edit_file\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: query_skill\n      - generic: \"用途: 当 catalog 里的简短 summary 不够用时，按名字拉一个已注册 skill 的完整元数据 (description / 参数契约 / affinity / 是否启用)；调不熟的工具前先查一查。 何时不用: 列出全部 skill 不要用本工具 (走 catalog / registry.list)；要执行 skill 直接调用对应工具名，不要先 query 再调 (浪费 token)；skill 不存在会返回 ok=false。 关键参数: name (必填, 已注册的 skill 名)。 示例: query_skill({\\\"name\\\": \\\"edit_file\\\"})\"\n    - menuitem \"r2-upload Upload files to Cloudflare R2, AWS S3, or any S3-compatible storage (like MinIO) and generate secure, time-limited presigned download links with configurable expiration, typically set to 5 minutes. Use when the user needs to upload a file to cloud storage and get a shareable link, or mentions R2, S3, presigned URLs, temporary links, or file uploads with expiration.\":\n      - generic: r2-upload\n      - generic: Upload files to Cloudflare R2, AWS S3, or any S3-compatible storage (like MinIO) and generate secure, time-limited presigned download links with configurable expiration, typically set to 5 minutes. Use when the user needs to upload a file to cloud storage and get a shareable link, or mentions R2, S3, presigned URLs, temporary links, or file uploads with expiration.\n    - menuitem \"reach_doctor Check SearXNG, GitHub, YouTube, Bilibili, RSS and browser-backed platform routes. Returns backend, availability, login requirement and repair context.\":\n      - generic: reach_doctor\n      - generic: Check SearXNG, GitHub, YouTube, Bilibili, RSS and browser-backed platform routes. Returns backend, availability, login requirement and repair context.\n    - 'menuitem \"read_background_output Poll stdout/stderr and status for a command started by `background_exec`.\"':\n      - generic: read_background_output\n      - generic: \"Poll stdout/stderr and status for a command started by `background_exec`.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"read_file 用途: 读取单个文件，按扩展名自动分发: 文本 (UTF-8, 默认 100KB / 2000 行硬上限) / 图片 (.png/.jpg/.jpeg/.webp/.gif → base64) / PDF (.pdf, 需要 pages 切片当 >10 页) / Notebook (.ipynb → 委托给 notebook_read)。 何时不用: 想找某段内容用 grep_text；只看前 N 行或某个范围用 read_file_range；按 pattern 找文件用 glob_files；不支持的二进制会拒读。支持 image/PDF/ipynb/PPTX/DOCX/XLSX/CSV/TSV。 关键参数: path (必填); offset/limit (文本按行切片); max_bytes (文本默认 102400); pages (PDF 切片 \\\"1-5\\\" / \\\"3\\\" / \\\"1-3,7,10-12\\\")。 示例: read_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/execution/suckers/builtins.py\\\", \\\"offset\\\": 0, \\\"limit\\\": 100}) · read_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"doc.pdf\\\", \\\"pages\\\": \\\"1-5\\\"}) · read_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"shot.png\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: read_file\n      - generic: \"用途: 读取单个文件，按扩展名自动分发: 文本 (UTF-8, 默认 100KB / 2000 行硬上限) / 图片 (.png/.jpg/.jpeg/.webp/.gif → base64) / PDF (.pdf, 需要 pages 切片当 >10 页) / Notebook (.ipynb → 委托给 notebook_read)。 何时不用: 想找某段内容用 grep_text；只看前 N 行或某个范围用 read_file_range；按 pattern 找文件用 glob_files；不支持的二进制会拒读。支持 image/PDF/ipynb/PPTX/DOCX/XLSX/CSV/TSV。 关键参数: path (必填); offset/limit (文本按行切片); max_bytes (文本默认 102400); pages (PDF 切片 \\\"1-5\\\" / \\\"3\\\" / \\\"1-3,7,10-12\\\")。 示例: read_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/execution/suckers/builtins.py\\\", \\\"offset\\\": 0, \\\"limit\\\": 100}) · read_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"doc.pdf\\\", \\\"pages\\\": \\\"1-5\\\"}) · read_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"shot.png\\\"})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"read_file_range 用途: 按 1-based 行号读文件的一段切片 (offset + limit, 上限 2000 行)；只想看「前 N 行」「某个区间」时省 token 的首选。 何时不用: 整文件不大用 read_file 一把读完；要找内容位置用 grep_text 后再来精读；要按 pattern 找用 glob_files；二进制 / 非 UTF-8 会拒读。 关键参数: path (必填); offset (默认 1, 起始行号); limit (默认 200, 上限 2000)。 示例: read_file_range({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/execution/suckers/builtins.py\\\", \\\"offset\\\": 100, \\\"limit\\\": 50})\"':\n      - generic: read_file_range\n      - generic: \"用途: 按 1-based 行号读文件的一段切片 (offset + limit, 上限 2000 行)；只想看「前 N 行」「某个区间」时省 token 的首选。 何时不用: 整文件不大用 read_file 一把读完；要找内容位置用 grep_text 后再来精读；要按 pattern 找用 glob_files；二进制 / 非 UTF-8 会拒读。 关键参数: path (必填); offset (默认 1, 起始行号); limit (默认 200, 上限 2000)。 示例: read_file_range({\\\"path\\\": \\\"runtime/execution/suckers/builtins.py\\\", \\\"offset\\\": 100, \\\"limit\\\": 50})\"\n    - menuitem \"read_shell_output Alias for read_background_output. Poll stdout/stderr and status for a command started by exec_shell(run_in_background=True) or background_exec.\":\n      - generic: read_shell_output\n      - generic: Alias for read_background_output. Poll stdout/stderr and status for a command started by exec_shell(run_in_background=True) or background_exec.\n    - 'menuitem \"recall Look up previously-saved notes from long-term memory. Keep their origin and unverified status when using them. CALL THIS AT THE START OF A TURN when the user references a project, person, or context you might have notes on — or anytime you''d otherwise say ''I don''t remember''. Args: {query?: string (substring filter), limit?: int (default 20, latest N if no query), scope?: ''all''|''agent''|''project''|''team''|''team_agent''|''global''}. Default scope is ''all'' visible tiers. Returns matching memory lines prefixed with their scope.\"':\n      - generic: recall\n      - generic: \"Look up previously-saved notes from long-term memory. Keep their origin and unverified status when using them. CALL THIS AT THE START OF A TURN when the user references a project, person, or context you might have notes on — or anytime you'd otherwise say 'I don't remember'. Args: {query?: string (substring filter), limit?: int (default 20, latest N if no query), scope?: 'all'|'agent'|'project'|'team'|'team_agent'|'global'}. Default scope is 'all' visible tiers. Returns matching memory lines prefixed with their scope.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"recall_scores Return your most recent per-turn quality scores (0.0/0.5/1.0 each, with a `reason` tag and the `soul_hash` that was active at score time). Useful to see if you''re trending well or poorly. The score is heuristic (computed from rounds / tool errors / interruption / token usage) — zero LLM cost. Args: {limit?: int, default 20}.\"':\n      - generic: recall_scores\n      - generic: \"Return your most recent per-turn quality scores (0.0/0.5/1.0 each, with a `reason` tag and the `soul_hash` that was active at score time). Useful to see if you're trending well or poorly. The score is heuristic (computed from rounds / tool errors / interruption / token usage) — zero LLM cost. Args: {limit?: int, default 20}.\"\n    - menuitem \"reconcile_candidate_patch Reconcile a patch_apply_started operation after interruption or an uncertain journal result. Pass only its host-issued operation_id. The host compares every file with durable old/new fingerprints, settles a fully applied transaction, restores known partial changes, and leaves externally changed files untouched.\":\n      - generic: reconcile_candidate_patch\n      - generic: Reconcile a patch_apply_started operation after interruption or an uncertain journal result. Pass only its host-issued operation_id. The host compares every file with durable old/new fingerprints, settles a fully applied transaction, restores known partial changes, and leaves externally changed files untouched.\n    - 'menuitem \"remember Save a durable note to long-term memory. Model-written notes remain unverified; they cannot certify execution or grant permission. CALL THIS WHEN the user mentions something worth remembering across future conversations: project names, deadlines, decisions made, key file paths, environment quirks, recurring preferences. Args: {fact: string, tags?: list[string], scope?: ''agent''|''project''|''team''|''team_agent''|''global''}. Default scope is ''agent''. Use ''team'' for shared Team decisions, ''team_agent'' for this member inside the Team, and ''project'' for repo/workspace conventions. Don''t use for transient context — only things that would still matter next week.\"':\n      - generic: remember\n      - generic: \"Save a durable note to long-term memory. Model-written notes remain unverified; they cannot certify execution or grant permission. CALL THIS WHEN the user mentions something worth remembering across future conversations: project names, deadlines, decisions made, key file paths, environment quirks, recurring preferences. Args: {fact: string, tags?: list[string], scope?: 'agent'|'project'|'team'|'team_agent'|'global'}. Default scope is 'agent'. Use 'team' for shared Team decisions, 'team_agent' for this member inside the Team, and 'project' for repo/workspace conventions. Don't use for transient context — only things that would still matter next week.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"repo-audit Deep analysis of Git history: identify frequently changed hotspot files, analyze code ownership by contributor, and scan for leaked secrets. Triggered when users ask about Git analysis, code hotspots, who owns what code, secret scanning, security audits of commit history, or optimizing code review assignments.\"':\n      - generic: repo-audit\n      - generic: \"Deep analysis of Git history: identify frequently changed hotspot files, analyze code ownership by contributor, and scan for leaked secrets. Triggered when users ask about Git analysis, code hotspots, who owns what code, secret scanning, security audits of commit history, or optimizing code review assignments.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"report-writing End-to-end long-form report creation — outline design, multi-chapter content writing, review, and assembly. Covers industry research, market analysis, policy briefs, technical reports, consulting deliverables, and any structured long-form non-fiction requiring research, argumentation, and citations. Outputs are delivered in Markdown (`.md`) format. Do NOT use for: academic papers (use paper-writing), creative fiction, blog posts, or short-form content under 2000 words.\"':\n      - generic: report-writing\n      - generic: \"End-to-end long-form report creation — outline design, multi-chapter content writing, review, and assembly. Covers industry research, market analysis, policy briefs, technical reports, consulting deliverables, and any structured long-form non-fiction requiring research, argumentation, and citations. Outputs are delivered in Markdown (`.md`) format. Do NOT use for: academic papers (use paper-writing), creative fiction, blog posts, or short-form content under 2000 words.\"\n    - menuitem \"resume-craft 优化简历，基于目标岗位JD进行关键词匹配分析，用STAR法则量化改写经历描述，并进行ATS友好度检查，最终输出一份针对性强、通过率高的优化简历。当用户请求优化、修改、润色简历，提到JD匹配、关键词、STAR法则、ATS，或询问“帮我改一下简历”、“这份简历能不能优化”、“简历怎么过ATS”等具体问题时触发。\":\n      - generic: resume-craft\n      - generic: 优化简历，基于目标岗位JD进行关键词匹配分析，用STAR法则量化改写经历描述，并进行ATS友好度检查，最终输出一份针对性强、通过率高的优化简历。当用户请求优化、修改、润色简历，提到JD匹配、关键词、STAR法则、ATS，或询问“帮我改一下简历”、“这份简历能不能优化”、“简历怎么过ATS”等具体问题时触发。\n    - 'menuitem \"revert_soul Roll your SOUL.md back N snapshots. Use this when you notice a recently-added lesson is causing regressions (over-cautious behavior, conflicting guidance, wrong tool choice, etc). The CURRENT state is snapshotted first under reason ''pre-revert-<reason>'' so the rollback is itself reversible. Args: {steps_back?: int (default 1), reason?: string (why you''re reverting · stored as the snapshot tag)}.\"':\n      - generic: revert_soul\n      - generic: \"Roll your SOUL.md back N snapshots. Use this when you notice a recently-added lesson is causing regressions (over-cautious behavior, conflicting guidance, wrong tool choice, etc). The CURRENT state is snapshotted first under reason 'pre-revert-<reason>' so the rollback is itself reversible. Args: {steps_back?: int (default 1), reason?: string (why you're reverting · stored as the snapshot tag)}.\"\n    - menuitem \"route-to-openapi Generates RESTful API documentation (OpenAPI 3.0 / Swagger spec) by scanning route definitions in code for Flask, FastAPI, Express, Gin, and other frameworks. Trigger when users ask about API documentation, OpenAPI, Swagger, endpoint docs, generating docs from code, or extracting endpoints.\":\n      - generic: route-to-openapi\n      - generic: Generates RESTful API documentation (OpenAPI 3.0 / Swagger spec) by scanning route definitions in code for Flask, FastAPI, Express, Gin, and other frameworks. Trigger when users ask about API documentation, OpenAPI, Swagger, endpoint docs, generating docs from code, or extracting endpoints.\n    - menuitem:\n      - generic: run_orchestration\n      - generic: \"Run a DETERMINISTIC multi-round discovery loop end-to-end in one call: fan out N workers per round, split their findings (one per line), de-duplicate against everything seen so far, and loop until no new findings arrive (or the round budget runs out) — optionally vote-verifying each finding. The control flow (looping, dedup, stop-when-dry) is code, not the model, so nothing is skipped. Use it for EXHAUSTIVE discovery where one pass isn't enough: 'find all the edge cases', 'enumerate every place X happens', 'gather everything known about Y'. This is the loop the flat per-turn cap normally forbids — it runs inside a bounded spawn budget instead. Args: {goal: string (what to discover), n?: int 1-6 workers/round (default 3), rounds?: int 1-5 (default 2), patience?: int 0-3 dry rounds tolerated before stopping (default 1), verify?: bool (default false — vote-verify each finding), synthesize?: bool (default false — fold the confirmed findings into ONE coherent answer via a final synthesizer; returned in `synthesis`), choices?: [keep,drop]-style ballot for verify, max_spawns?: int total spawn budget (auto-sized, capped at 48), agent_id?: worker role, or a LIST of roles rotated across workers for diverse lenses, e.g. [researcher, explorer, critic] (default researcher)}. Returns: {ok, goal, collected:[...], confirmed:[...] (== collected unless verify), count, rounds_run, fresh_per_round:[...], verified, unverified, synthesis (str, '' unless synthesize), shared (bool — findings published to the turn blackboard), inherited (int — findings seeded from siblings' blackboard entries), stopped_reason (rounds|dry|budget|cap), budget_used, max_spawns, failures (list of {role, error, error_type} — de-duplicated sub-agent failure summaries, empty when every worker succeeded), failure_count (int — raw total of failed sub-agent runs), note (str — a warning when any sub-agent failed; '' otherwise)}. Coordination: findings are auto-shared on the turn's blackboard, so a sibling agent or a later orchestration on the same goal builds on them instead of re-discovering — enforced by the harness, no manual bb_write needed. Budget: one orchestration costs ONE against the 5/turn delegation cap; its internal fan-outs/votes draw from the bounded spawn budget, not the turn cap. Reserve it for genuinely multi-round work.\"\n    - menuitem:\n      - generic: run_pipeline\n      - generic: \"Process a list of items through ORDERED STAGES without waiting for all items to complete each stage before advancing — item A can be in stage 3 while item B is still in stage 1. Use it when: - You have N independent items (files, URLs, tasks) that each need the SAME sequence of specialist passes (find → review → fix, or extract → classify → summarise). - Stages are sequential PER ITEM (each stage needs the previous output for that item), but items themselves are independent. - You want true pipeline throughput: wall-clock = max(slowest item chain), not sum of slowest-per-stage. Stage prompt templates use: {item} — the original item value {prev} — previous stage's output for this item (empty for stage 0) {stage0_output}, {stage1_output}, ... — any earlier stage's output A failed stage halts that item's chain; remaining stages for that item are skipped. Other items continue. Args: {items: list[str|dict] (up to 16), stages: list[{prompt_template: str, agent_id?: str}] (up to 4 stages), default_agent_id?: str (used when stage omits agent_id, default researcher), timeout_s?: int (per-subagent, default 900)}. Returns: {ok, results:[{item, stages:[{stage, agent_id, output, ok}], final_output, ok}], success_count, failure_count, total, stages_run}. Budget: one pipeline costs ONE against the 5/turn delegation cap; item × stage spawn budget is managed internally.\"\n    - menuitem \"run_tests Run project tests (auto-detects pytest/vitest/npm test). Tests have no default wall-clock limit, stream progress while running, and remain cancellable; pass a positive timeout_s only for an explicit deadline.\":\n      - generic: run_tests\n      - generic: Run project tests (auto-detects pytest/vitest/npm test). Tests have no default wall-clock limit, stream progress while running, and remain cancellable; pass a positive timeout_s only for an explicit deadline.\n    - menuitem \"rust-browser-pilot 基于 Rust 的高性能浏览器自动化工具，通过 Chrome DevTools 协议直接驱动浏览器，执行 DOM 提取、页面截图、表单填写、会话管理和站点地图分析等操作。启动速度和内存效率远超 Puppeteer 与 Selenium，非常适合网页抓取、自动化测试和需要复杂交互的场景。当用户需要自动化浏览器任务、提及网页抓取、自动化测试、DOM 提取、页面截图、表单填写、会话管理、站点地图分析，或比较 Puppeteer/Selenium 性能时触发。\":\n      - generic: rust-browser-pilot\n      - generic: 基于 Rust 的高性能浏览器自动化工具，通过 Chrome DevTools 协议直接驱动浏览器，执行 DOM 提取、页面截图、表单填写、会话管理和站点地图分析等操作。启动速度和内存效率远超 Puppeteer 与 Selenium，非常适合网页抓取、自动化测试和需要复杂交互的场景。当用户需要自动化浏览器任务、提及网页抓取、自动化测试、DOM 提取、页面截图、表单填写、会话管理、站点地图分析，或比较 Puppeteer/Selenium 性能时触发。\n    - 'menuitem \"schedule_task Schedule a future agent turn. Persists into the same cron store the settings UI uses so model-scheduled tasks show up alongside user-created ones. Authenticated tasks are bound to the current server-resolved tenant and owner. Args: {prompt: str (required), cron_expression: 5-field cron string for recurring runs, fire_at: ISO 8601 timestamp with timezone offset for one-shot, recurring: bool (default true), name: optional task id (auto-generated if omitted), channel_id/thread_id: optional IM delivery target (defaults to the conversation this task is scheduled from, so a reminder/subscription auto-pushes its result back over IM). Supply exactly one of cron_expression / fire_at. Returns {ok, task_id, next_run_at}.\"':\n      - generic: schedule_task\n      - generic: \"Schedule a future agent turn. Persists into the same cron store the settings UI uses so model-scheduled tasks show up alongside user-created ones. Authenticated tasks are bound to the current server-resolved tenant and owner. Args: {prompt: str (required), cron_expression: 5-field cron string for recurring runs, fire_at: ISO 8601 timestamp with timezone offset for one-shot, recurring: bool (default true), name: optional task id (auto-generated if omitted), channel_id/thread_id: optional IM delivery target (defaults to the conversation this task is scheduled from, so a reminder/subscription auto-pushes its result back over IM). Supply exactly one of cron_expression / fire_at. Returns {ok, task_id, next_run_at}.\"\n    - menuitem \"screen_capture Capture screen (or region [x,y,w,h]) to PNG · path_guard enforced.\":\n      - generic: screen_capture\n      - generic: Capture screen (or region [x,y,w,h]) to PNG · path_guard enforced.\n    - menuitem \"screen_info Return screen width/height and current cursor position.\":\n      - generic: screen_info\n      - generic: Return screen width/height and current cursor position.\n    - menuitem \"screenshot_web_full_page Capture a full-page screenshot of a URL.\":\n      - generic: screenshot_web_full_page\n      - generic: Capture a full-page screenshot of a URL.\n    - 'menuitem \"search_capabilities Search package-level capabilities first: plugins, skill packs, and meta-skill packages. Use this before searching low-level skills when the task sounds like a product capability, plugin, workflow, or tool box.\"':\n      - generic: search_capabilities\n      - generic: \"Search package-level capabilities first: plugins, skill packs, and meta-skill packages. Use this before searching low-level skills when the task sounds like a product capability, plugin, workflow, or tool box.\"\n    - menuitem \"search_image_by_image Reverse image search through a configured provider.\":\n      - generic: search_image_by_image\n      - generic: Reverse image search through a configured provider.\n    - menuitem \"search_image_by_text Search the web for image candidates by text query.\":\n      - generic: search_image_by_text\n      - generic: Search the web for image candidates by text query.\n    - 'menuitem \"search_skills Purpose: search the entire registered skill catalog by keyword when the compact prompt catalog was truncated or you do not know the exact skill name. Search matches name, summary, affinity, and description, then returns compact candidates. Call query_skill(name=...) for full details before using an unfamiliar candidate. When not to use: if the needed skill is already visible and its parameters are obvious; call that skill directly. Key params: query (keyword), limit (1-25, default 10), include_disabled (default false). Example: search_skills({\\\"query\\\": \\\"subagent parallel\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: search_skills\n      - generic: \"Purpose: search the entire registered skill catalog by keyword when the compact prompt catalog was truncated or you do not know the exact skill name. Search matches name, summary, affinity, and description, then returns compact candidates. Call query_skill(name=...) for full details before using an unfamiliar candidate. When not to use: if the needed skill is already visible and its parameters are obvious; call that skill directly. Key params: query (keyword), limit (1-25, default 10), include_disabled (default false). Example: search_skills({\\\"query\\\": \\\"subagent parallel\\\"})\"\n    - menuitem \"seedance-video-generate 使用火山引擎 Seedance 模型从文字提示、图像或参考素材生成视频。支持多种视频风格、时长和分辨率。当用户需要生成视频内容、动画、广告片或任何动态视觉内容时调用此技能。\":\n      - generic: seedance-video-generate\n      - generic: 使用火山引擎 Seedance 模型从文字提示、图像或参考素材生成视频。支持多种视频风格、时长和分辨率。当用户需要生成视频内容、动画、广告片或任何动态视觉内容时调用此技能。\n    - menuitem \"seedream-image-generate 使用火山引擎 Seedream 模型从文字描述生成高质量图像，支持多种艺术风格和宽高比。当用户需要生成图片、插画、设计素材或任何视觉内容时调用此技能。\":\n      - generic: seedream-image-generate\n      - generic: 使用火山引擎 Seedream 模型从文字描述生成高质量图像，支持多种艺术风格和宽高比。当用户需要生成图片、插画、设计素材或任何视觉内容时调用此技能。\n    - menuitem \"seo-audit When the user wants to audit, review, or diagnose SEO issues on their site. Also use when the user mentions \\\"SEO audit,\\\" \\\"technical SEO,\\\" \\\"why am I not ranking,\\\" \\\"SEO issues,\\\" \\\"on-page SEO,\\\" \\\"meta tags review,\\\" \\\"SEO health check,\\\" \\\"my traffic dropped,\\\" \\\"lost rankings,\\\" \\\"not showing up in Google,\\\" \\\"site isn't ranking,\\\" \\\"Google update hit me,\\\" \\\"page speed,\\\" \\\"core web vitals,\\\" \\\"crawl errors,\\\" or \\\"indexing issues.\\\" Use this even if the user just says something vague like \\\"my SEO is bad\\\" or \\\"help with SEO\\\" — start with an audit.\":\n      - generic: seo-audit\n      - generic: When the user wants to audit, review, or diagnose SEO issues on their site. Also use when the user mentions \"SEO audit,\" \"technical SEO,\" \"why am I not ranking,\" \"SEO issues,\" \"on-page SEO,\" \"meta tags review,\" \"SEO health check,\" \"my traffic dropped,\" \"lost rankings,\" \"not showing up in Google,\" \"site isn't ranking,\" \"Google update hit me,\" \"page speed,\" \"core web vitals,\" \"crawl errors,\" or \"indexing issues.\" Use this even if the user just says something vague like \"my SEO is bad\" or \"help with SEO\" — start with an audit.\n    - menuitem \"smart-web-scraper 基于 Playwright 智能爬取网页内容，内置绕过 Cloudflare 等反爬机制的能力，提供简单模式和隐身模式两种方案以应对不同反爬强度，输出网页标题、文本内容和截图。当用户需要抓取动态网页、获取被保护网站的数据，或提到爬虫、反爬虫、Cloudflare、网页截图、JavaScript渲染等关键词时触发。\":\n      - generic: smart-web-scraper\n      - generic: 基于 Playwright 智能爬取网页内容，内置绕过 Cloudflare 等反爬机制的能力，提供简单模式和隐身模式两种方案以应对不同反爬强度，输出网页标题、文本内容和截图。当用户需要抓取动态网页、获取被保护网站的数据，或提到爬虫、反爬虫、Cloudflare、网页截图、JavaScript渲染等关键词时触发。\n    - menuitem \"speech-synthesis 将文本转换为高质量语音，支持多语言、多种音色，可调节语速、音调和音量，并生成字幕，输出MP3音频文件。当你需要朗读文本（比如文章、消息）、为视频或演示文稿生成配音，或直接提到“TTS”、“文字转语音”、“配音”、“朗读”时，就会使用这个技能。\":\n      - generic: speech-synthesis\n      - generic: 将文本转换为高质量语音，支持多语言、多种音色，可调节语速、音调和音量，并生成字幕，输出MP3音频文件。当你需要朗读文本（比如文章、消息）、为视频或演示文稿生成配音，或直接提到“TTS”、“文字转语音”、“配音”、“朗读”时，就会使用这个技能。\n    - menuitem \"sql-insight Translate natural language to SQL, optimize query performance, and interpret EXPLAIN plans for SQLite and PostgreSQL. Triggered when users ask to convert questions into SQL, improve slow queries, tune indexes, analyze execution plans, or mention keywords like NL2SQL, query tuning, or full table scan.\":\n      - generic: sql-insight\n      - generic: Translate natural language to SQL, optimize query performance, and interpret EXPLAIN plans for SQLite and PostgreSQL. Triggered when users ask to convert questions into SQL, improve slow queries, tune indexes, analyze execution plans, or mention keywords like NL2SQL, query tuning, or full table scan.\n    - menuitem \"sunlight-analysis 生成太阳轨迹图，计算实时太阳位置，分析建筑阴影投射范围与全年日照时数，并提供热舒适度评估，适用于建筑设计与场地环境分析。当用户询问太阳位置、请求绘制太阳轨迹、分析建筑阴影、计算全年日照时间、评估热舒适度或进行地形阴影分析时触发。\":\n      - generic: sunlight-analysis\n      - generic: 生成太阳轨迹图，计算实时太阳位置，分析建筑阴影投射范围与全年日照时数，并提供热舒适度评估，适用于建筑设计与场地环境分析。当用户询问太阳位置、请求绘制太阳轨迹、分析建筑阴影、计算全年日照时间、评估热舒适度或进行地形阴影分析时触发。\n    - menuitem \"terraform-deploy-pitfalls Operational traps for Terraform provisioners, multi-environment isolation, and zero-to-deployment reliability. Covers provisioner timing races, SSH connection conflicts, DNS record duplication, volume permissions, database bootstrap gaps, snapshot cross-contamination, Cloudflare credential format errors, hardcoded domains in Caddyfiles/compose, and init-data-only-on-first-boot pitfalls. Activate when writing null_resource provisioners, creating multi-environment Terraform setups, debugging containers that are Restarting/unhealthy after terraform apply, setting up fresh instances with cloud-init, or any IaC code that SSHs into remote hosts. Also activate when the user mentions terraform plan/apply errors, provisioner failures, infrastructure drift, TLS certificate errors, or Caddy/gateway configuration.\":\n      - generic: terraform-deploy-pitfalls\n      - generic: Operational traps for Terraform provisioners, multi-environment isolation, and zero-to-deployment reliability. Covers provisioner timing races, SSH connection conflicts, DNS record duplication, volume permissions, database bootstrap gaps, snapshot cross-contamination, Cloudflare credential format errors, hardcoded domains in Caddyfiles/compose, and init-data-only-on-first-boot pitfalls. Activate when writing null_resource provisioners, creating multi-environment Terraform setups, debugging containers that are Restarting/unhealthy after terraform apply, setting up fresh instances with cloud-init, or any IaC code that SSHs into remote hosts. Also activate when the user mentions terraform plan/apply errors, provisioner failures, infrastructure drift, TLS certificate errors, or Caddy/gateway configuration.\n    - menuitem \"test-driven-dev Test-driven development with red-green-refactor loop. Use when user wants to build features or fix bugs using TDD, mentions \\\"red-green-refactor\\\", wants integration tests, or asks for test-first development.\":\n      - generic: test-driven-dev\n      - generic: Test-driven development with red-green-refactor loop. Use when user wants to build features or fix bugs using TDD, mentions \"red-green-refactor\", wants integration tests, or asks for test-first development.\n    - 'menuitem \"todo_read 用途: 读取当前 turn / thread 的实时任务计划 (上次 todo_write 的最新快照)；恢复长任务、检查清单状态时调用。 何时不用: 想新建或更新任务清单用 todo_write (传完整新列表)；想看某个 skill 的元数据用 query_skill；这不是给用户的「最终答复」，只是内部进度查询。 关键参数: 无必填参数 (按当前会话作用域自动定位)。 示例: todo_read({})\"':\n      - generic: todo_read\n      - generic: \"用途: 读取当前 turn / thread 的实时任务计划 (上次 todo_write 的最新快照)；恢复长任务、检查清单状态时调用。 何时不用: 想新建或更新任务清单用 todo_write (传完整新列表)；想看某个 skill 的元数据用 query_skill；这不是给用户的「最终答复」，只是内部进度查询。 关键参数: 无必填参数 (按当前会话作用域自动定位)。 示例: todo_read({})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"todo_write 用途: 维护 agent 的任务清单 (实时进度面板) — 多步任务一开始全列出 (pending)，每完成 / 切换一步重传完整列表 (一项 in_progress, 完成的 completed)。 何时不用: 只是看当前清单用 todo_read；单步小任务不必拆；不要拿这个工具传 diff (必须传完整列表)；最终答复仍走正常输出，不要塞这里。 关键参数: items (必填, list[{id?, content, status: pending|in_progress|completed, activeForm}]; todos 是兼容别名; 同时只能一个 in_progress, 否则后续被降级为 pending)。首次可省略 id，后续更新应原样保留返回的 id。 示例: todo_write({\\\"items\\\": [{\\\"id\\\": \\\"tests\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Run tests\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"in_progress\\\", \\\"activeForm\\\": \\\"Running tests\\\"}]})\"':\n      - generic: todo_write\n      - generic: \"用途: 维护 agent 的任务清单 (实时进度面板) — 多步任务一开始全列出 (pending)，每完成 / 切换一步重传完整列表 (一项 in_progress, 完成的 completed)。 何时不用: 只是看当前清单用 todo_read；单步小任务不必拆；不要拿这个工具传 diff (必须传完整列表)；最终答复仍走正常输出，不要塞这里。 关键参数: items (必填, list[{id?, content, status: pending|in_progress|completed, activeForm}]; todos 是兼容别名; 同时只能一个 in_progress, 否则后续被降级为 pending)。首次可省略 id，后续更新应原样保留返回的 id。 示例: todo_write({\\\"items\\\": [{\\\"id\\\": \\\"tests\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Run tests\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"in_progress\\\", \\\"activeForm\\\": \\\"Running tests\\\"}]})\"\n    - menuitem:\n      - generic: tournament\n      - generic: \"Attempt the SAME goal N independent times, each in its OWN isolated git worktree (no collisions), then have an independent panel VOTE on which result is best — best-of-N with a judge. Builds on octopus's worktree isolation (the candidates) plus call_agent_vote (the judge); selection is deterministic code. NEVER auto-applies: the winning diff and durable patch reference are returned for review and an explicit application decision. Each candidate starts from the approved project's working files, including uncommitted changes. Use it when one attempt is unreliable and the solution space is wide, so divergent tries help: 'implement X — try a few approaches and keep the best', 'refactor this several ways and pick the cleanest'. Costly (N full coding sub-agents + voters) — reserve it for genuinely high-value or ambiguous work. Args: {goal: string (what each candidate should accomplish), n?: int 2-5 candidates (default 3), agent_id?: worker role (default worktree_writer), judge_n?: int 2-5 voters (default 3), repo_root?: path (must match the host-approved project), input_files?: list[str], output_files?: list[str], max_workers?: int (default 4), timeout_s?: int (per child; the parent deadline still applies)}. Returns: {ok, goal, decided_by (judge|only_candidate|judge_abstained|none), candidate_count, viable_count, winner:{id, files, diff, worktree}, candidates:[{id, ok, viable, files, error, worktree?}], selection_id, spawns_used, retry_allowed:false, note}. Failed candidates retain their patch or retained_workspace coordinates. Producers and read-only judges share the spawn budget, deadline and cancellation. Do not automatically repeat a tournament after a partial or interrupted run.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"tree 用途: 递归打出目录结构 (默认 3 层, 上限 8 层 / 1000 节点)；用于第一次进项目时建立全局认知。 何时不用: 只看一层用 list_cwd 更省 token；按 pattern 找文件用 glob_files；按内容找用 grep_text；要文件元数据用 file_stats。 关键参数: root (默认 ''.''); max_depth (默认 3, 上限 8); max_nodes (默认 1000); include_hidden (默认 False)。 示例: tree({\\\"root\\\": \\\"runtime\\\", \\\"max_depth\\\": 2})\"':\n      - generic: tree\n      - generic: \"用途: 递归打出目录结构 (默认 3 层, 上限 8 层 / 1000 节点)；用于第一次进项目时建立全局认知。 何时不用: 只看一层用 list_cwd 更省 token；按 pattern 找文件用 glob_files；按内容找用 grep_text；要文件元数据用 file_stats。 关键参数: root (默认 '.'); max_depth (默认 3, 上限 8); max_nodes (默认 1000); include_hidden (默认 False)。 示例: tree({\\\"root\\\": \\\"runtime\\\", \\\"max_depth\\\": 2})\"\n    - menuitem \"typescript-best-practices TypeScript 最佳实践技能，包含类型安全、泛型、类型推断、严格模式配置。在编写 TypeScript 代码或类型定义时调用。\":\n      - generic: typescript-best-practices\n      - generic: TypeScript 最佳实践技能，包含类型安全、泛型、类型推断、严格模式配置。在编写 TypeScript 代码或类型定义时调用。\n    - menuitem \"ui-blueprint 从参考 UI 截图或设计稿中提取完整的设计系统，生成包含配色、字体、组件和间距规范的设计文档，并最终产出可直接用于实现、风格一致的 MVP 界面提示词。当用户提供 UI 截图并希望提取设计规范、构建设计系统文档、或需要基于参考风格创建新界面时触发。\":\n      - generic: ui-blueprint\n      - generic: 从参考 UI 截图或设计稿中提取完整的设计系统，生成包含配色、字体、组件和间距规范的设计文档，并最终产出可直接用于实现、风格一致的 MVP 界面提示词。当用户提供 UI 截图并希望提取设计规范、构建设计系统文档、或需要基于参考风格创建新界面时触发。\n    - 'menuitem \"update_soul Append a SELF-learned lesson to your own SOUL.md. The lesson is auto-loaded into your system prompt on next session boot, so this is how you get smarter over time. Use ONLY for durable insights about your own work style — workarounds that actually worked, approaches that failed and why, quirks of a tool''s args that bit you, multi-step patterns worth repeating. NOT for facts about the world (use `remember`) or about the user (use `note_user`). Every successful write is auto-snapshotted to `.soul_history/` so you can `revert_soul` if a lesson turns out to hurt later turns. Args: {lesson: imperative one-liner, tag?: short category like ''tooling'' / ''workflow'' / ''mistake''}.\"':\n      - generic: update_soul\n      - generic: \"Append a SELF-learned lesson to your own SOUL.md. The lesson is auto-loaded into your system prompt on next session boot, so this is how you get smarter over time. Use ONLY for durable insights about your own work style — workarounds that actually worked, approaches that failed and why, quirks of a tool's args that bit you, multi-step patterns worth repeating. NOT for facts about the world (use `remember`) or about the user (use `note_user`). Every successful write is auto-snapshotted to `.soul_history/` so you can `revert_soul` if a lesson turns out to hurt later turns. Args: {lesson: imperative one-liner, tag?: short category like 'tooling' / 'workflow' / 'mistake'}.\"\n    - menuitem \"use_capability Use a plugin or skill pack as a top-level capability. Without action it returns the package's registered actions and guidance. With action and args it runs that registered child action internally, so the model does not need to see every child tool in the first tool list.\":\n      - generic: use_capability\n      - generic: Use a plugin or skill pack as a top-level capability. Without action it returns the package's registered actions and guidance. With action and args it runs that registered child action internally, so the model does not need to see every child tool in the first tool list.\n    - menuitem \"use_chatgpt_connector Use an OpenAI/ChatGPT App connector already enabled by the current user. Pass the exact app_id shown in Coder settings and a concrete request. Authentication remains inside Codex App Server; connector side effects require the normal Octopus approval flow.\":\n      - generic: use_chatgpt_connector\n      - generic: Use an OpenAI/ChatGPT App connector already enabled by the current user. Pass the exact app_id shown in Coder settings and a concrete request. Authentication remains inside Codex App Server; connector side effects require the normal Octopus approval flow.\n    - menuitem:\n      - generic: verdict_repair\n      - generic: \"Run a task through a CLOSED quality loop in one call: a worker produces a result, an independent panel VOTES pass/fail on it, and a rejection drives a corrected re-attempt that is FED the reviewers' critique — produce → judge → rewrite → re-judge, bounded. The loop (stop-on-pass, bound, feeding the critique forward) is deterministic code, not the model, so a FAIL actually triggers a fix instead of just shipping. Use it when correctness matters more than speed and a single attempt isn't trustworthy: 'write this function AND make sure it's right', 'draft the migration and have it reviewed until it passes', 'answer this, but verify before returning'. Args: {task: string (what to accomplish), agent_id?: worker role (default general), judge_n?: int 2-5 voters on the gate (default 3), max_repairs?: int 0-4 corrective re-attempts (default 2), choices?: [accept,reject]-style ballot where the FIRST label means accept (default [pass,fail])}. Returns: {ok, task, passed (bool — did it clear the gate), repaired (bool — only reached pass AFTER a repair), output (the accepted/best result), attempts, verdict, confidence, rounds:[{attempt, passed, verdict, critique}], max_spawns}. Budget: one call costs ONE against the 5/turn delegation cap; its internal produce/judge fan-outs draw from a bounded spawn budget.\"\n    - menuitem \"vibecoding-general-swarm General-purpose coding orchestration. MANDATORY for ANY coding task not covered by vibecoding-webapp-swarm. Skip ONLY if the task matches vibecoding-webapp-swarm or is entirely non-coding.\":\n      - generic: vibecoding-general-swarm\n      - generic: General-purpose coding orchestration. MANDATORY for ANY coding task not covered by vibecoding-webapp-swarm. Skip ONLY if the task matches vibecoding-webapp-swarm or is entirely non-coding.\n    - 'menuitem \"vibecoding-webapp-swarm Build any web-based project: websites, landing pages, web apps, dashboards, browser games, portfolios, and interactive experiences. Design-first React workflow. Skip if the user explicitly requests a non-React framework (Vue, Svelte, Angular, vanilla HTML) or the task is unrelated to web UI (CLI tools, scripts, data pipelines).\"':\n      - generic: vibecoding-webapp-swarm\n      - generic: \"Build any web-based project: websites, landing pages, web apps, dashboards, browser games, portfolios, and interactive experiences. Design-first React workflow. Skip if the user explicitly requests a non-React framework (Vue, Svelte, Angular, vanilla HTML) or the task is unrelated to web UI (CLI tools, scripts, data pipelines).\"\n    - 'menuitem \"web_fetch 用途: 给一个 URL + 一个问题，由廉价 LLM 在页面正文里抽出答案；只把 answer 字符串回给主模型，不再让主模型啃 50KB 原始 HTML。 何时不用: 只想拿原文 / 自己解析用 fetch_url(extract=true)；不知道目标网址先用 web_search；要本地文件 Q&A 用 read_file 自己问。 关键参数: url (必填); prompt (必填, 你想从页面里得到的答案); max_chars (送进 LLM 的正文上限, 默认 16000); cheap_model (可选, 留空走 web_fetch_default_model)。 示例: web_fetch({\\\"url\\\": \\\"https://docs.example.com/limits\\\", \\\"prompt\\\": \\\"What is the rate limit?\\\"})\"':\n      - generic: web_fetch\n      - generic: \"用途: 给一个 URL + 一个问题，由廉价 LLM 在页面正文里抽出答案；只把 answer 字符串回给主模型，不再让主模型啃 50KB 原始 HTML。 何时不用: 只想拿原文 / 自己解析用 fetch_url(extract=true)；不知道目标网址先用 web_search；要本地文件 Q&A 用 read_file 自己问。 关键参数: url (必填); prompt (必填, 你想从页面里得到的答案); max_chars (送进 LLM 的正文上限, 默认 16000); cheap_model (可选, 留空走 web_fetch_default_model)。 示例: web_fetch({\\\"url\\\": \\\"https://docs.example.com/limits\\\", \\\"prompt\\\": \\\"What is the rate limit?\\\"})\"\n    - 'menuitem \"web_search 用途: 网上检索 — 任何「需要谷歌一下」的查询 (新闻、价格、定义、X 的现状、近期事件、产品对比) 都走这里；返回结构化 [{title, url, snippet}]。 何时不用: 已经知道具体 URL 直接读用 fetch_url；不要用 exec_shell 跑 curl/wget 拿 HTML (没法解析)；查本地代码/配置用 grep_text 或 glob_files。 关键参数: query (必填); max_results (默认 5); backend (可选, 留空时按环境变量自动选 doubao/tavily/brave/serper/searxng/ddg)。 路由提示: 通常不要填写 backend，让系统按当前可用凭据自动选择和故障降级；仅当用户明确要求某个搜索源时再指定。 研究要求: 复杂调研至少使用两组不同关键词，优先读取 source_quality=primary 的原始来源；搜索摘要只用于发现候选 URL，关键结论必须再用 web_fetch 核验正文。 示例: web_search({\\\"query\\\": \\\"langgraph 0.2 release notes\\\", \\\"max_results\\\": 5})\"':\n      - generic: web_search\n      - generic: \"用途: 网上检索 — 任何「需要谷歌一下」的查询 (新闻、价格、定义、X 的现状、近期事件、产品对比) 都走这里；返回结构化 [{title, url, snippet}]。 何时不用: 已经知道具体 URL 直接读用 fetch_url；不要用 exec_shell 跑 curl/wget 拿 HTML (没法解析)；查本地代码/配置用 grep_text 或 glob_files。 关键参数: query (必填); max_results (默认 5); backend (可选, 留空时按环境变量自动选 doubao/tavily/brave/serper/searxng/ddg)。 路由提示: 通常不要填写 backend，让系统按当前可用凭据自动选择和故障降级；仅当用户明确要求某个搜索源时再指定。 研究要求: 复杂调研至少使用两组不同关键词，优先读取 source_quality=primary 的原始来源；搜索摘要只用于发现候选 URL，关键结论必须再用 web_fetch 核验正文。 示例: web_search({\\\"query\\\": \\\"langgraph 0.2 release notes\\\", \\\"max_results\\\": 5})\"\n    - menuitem \"web-security-audit 基于 OWASP Top 10 (2021) 标准提供代码安全审查，逐项检查 SQL 注入、XSS、SSRF、访问控制、加密失败等常见漏洞，并给出具体的漏洞代码示例与修复方案。当用户需要代码安全审查、安全加固、渗透测试辅助，或提及 OWASP、安全检查、SQL 注入、XSS、代码审计、安全清单等关键词时触发此技能。\":\n      - generic: web-security-audit\n      - generic: 基于 OWASP Top 10 (2021) 标准提供代码安全审查，逐项检查 SQL 注入、XSS、SSRF、访问控制、加密失败等常见漏洞，并给出具体的漏洞代码示例与修复方案。当用户需要代码安全审查、安全加固、渗透测试辅助，或提及 OWASP、安全检查、SQL 注入、XSS、代码审计、安全清单等关键词时触发此技能。\n    - menuitem \"webapp-building Tools for building modern React webapps with TypeScript, Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui. Best suited for applications with complex UI components and state management. Supports optional templates for specialized requirement.\":\n      - generic: webapp-building\n      - generic: Tools for building modern React webapps with TypeScript, Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui. Best suited for applications with complex UI components and state management. Supports optional templates for specialized requirement.\n    - menuitem \"website_version_manager Snapshot/list/restore/delete local website project versions.\":\n      - generic: website_version_manager\n      - generic: Snapshot/list/restore/delete local website project versions.\n    - menuitem \"whale_eye.read 读图并输出中文判读。把一张截图(本地图片路径 image,或 url 由本工具截图)交给 agnes 视觉模型做 UI 视觉回归:检查布局溢出/重叠/错位、文案截断、对比度/样式问题、加载态等。返回中文判读文本,agent 据此判断页面渲染是否正常。纯文本模型用它'看'图。\":\n      - generic: whale_eye.read\n      - generic: 读图并输出中文判读。把一张截图(本地图片路径 image,或 url 由本工具截图)交给 agnes 视觉模型做 UI 视觉回归:检查布局溢出/重叠/错位、文案截断、对比度/样式问题、加载态等。返回中文判读文本,agent 据此判断页面渲染是否正常。纯文本模型用它'看'图。\n    - menuitem \"whatsapp-integration WhatsApp integration for sending messages, managing contacts, and interacting with chats and groups. Use when the user wants to send a WhatsApp message, check a contact, read a chat, or perform any other action related to WhatsApp data.\":\n      - generic: whatsapp-integration\n      - generic: WhatsApp integration for sending messages, managing contacts, and interacting with chats and groups. Use when the user wants to send a WhatsApp message, check a contact, read a chat, or perform any other action related to WhatsApp data.\n    - menuitem:\n      - generic: workflow\n      - generic: \"Run a model-authored Python orchestration script that fans out subagents and returns the script's final JSON value. The script executes in an isolated worker process against a SMALL restricted vocabulary — no imports, no file/network access, no introspection. Attribute access is allowed only on non-dunder names (e.g. `s.strip()`, `d.items()`); `x.__class__`-style dunder access, imports, classes and generators are rejected at parse time. Available globals: - `args` — the plain JSON `args` object (a dict; use `args[\\\"key\\\"]`). - `agent(prompt, opts?)` — run one isolated subagent and return its final text (or structured value when `opts[\\\"schema\\\"]` is set). Options: `label` (display), `phase` (grouping), `schema` (JSON Schema object — only `{\\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\", ...}` is supported; the child returns the validated value), `provider` (optional subagent role/agent id override), `model` (optional child model override). A child that fails for its own reasons returns `None` — filter it out. - `phase(title)` — announce a progress phase. - `log(message)` — narrate a progress line. - `parallel([thunk, ...])` — run zero-argument thunks concurrently; an ordinary thunk failure becomes `None`, a fatal error (bad option, cap tripped, infrastructure fault) aborts the whole script. - `pipeline(items, *stages)` — run per-item stage chains concurrently; an ordinary stage failure drops THAT item to `None`, fatals abort. The script ends with `return <json-value>` (top-level `await` allowed). The return value must be plain JSON data. Do NOT assign a top-level `meta` variable — meta rides this call's `meta` parameter. `meta` = `{\\\"name\\\": kebab-case-name, \\\"description\\\": one-line, \\\"whenToUse\\\"?, \\\"phases\\\"?}`. Phases are progress annotations only. Caps: `max_total_agents` (per-run child ceiling, default engine-wide), concurrent agent calls bounded by the engine, per-call item cap for parallel/pipeline. Cancellation is cooperative at hook boundaries. Returns `{runId, agentsStarted, result}`. Use when a task decomposes into an orchestrated fan-out (research lanes, parallel review, staged pipelines) that fixed `call_agent_parallel` envelopes cannot express.\"\n    - 'menuitem \"write_text_file 用途: 把 UTF-8 文本完整写入一个新文件；首选用于「创建新文件」场景。会受 sandbox_dir 路径校验保护。 何时不用: 要修改已有文件请用 edit_file (按唯一片段) 或 multi_edit_file (批量精确替换)；要追加内容用 append_text_file；要写二进制不要用本工具。 关键参数: path (必填); content (必填); overwrite (默认 False — 文件已存在时返回错误); max_bytes (默认 1MB)。 示例: write_text_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"notes.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# hello\\\\n\\\", \\\"overwrite\\\": false})\"':\n      - generic: write_text_file\n      - generic: \"用途: 把 UTF-8 文本完整写入一个新文件；首选用于「创建新文件」场景。会受 sandbox_dir 路径校验保护。 何时不用: 要修改已有文件请用 edit_file (按唯一片段) 或 multi_edit_file (批量精确替换)；要追加内容用 append_text_file；要写二进制不要用本工具。 关键参数: path (必填); content (必填); overwrite (默认 False — 文件已存在时返回错误); max_bytes (默认 1MB)。 示例: write_text_file({\\\"path\\\": \\\"notes.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# hello\\\\n\\\", \\\"overwrite\\\": false})\"\n    - separator\n    - menuitem \"管理技能\":\n      - text: 管理技能\n  - separator\n  - menuitem \"建立项目计划\":\n    - text: 建立项目计划"